-- Employment Insurance Regulations (SOR/96-332), regulations 35 to 57 -- THE SEAT LAYER (piece er3).
-- Written by the piece agent er3 (Sonnet 5.5) on 2026-10-24 from the unofficial plain-text rendering
-- SOR-96-332.txt; nothing here is claimed to be verified against the official text.
--
-- SEAT: a person who has lost work, or cannot work because of sickness, pregnancy, caring for a child or a family
-- member, or who is self-employed or a fisher, asking whether they qualify for Employment Insurance benefits, how
-- many hours or weeks they need, how much they would receive and for how long, and what they must do or tell the
-- Commission. For regulations 35 to 57 that person asks: does what I received count as earnings, what is it worth
-- and to which weeks does it go; is my employer's plan one whose payments are left out; what is deducted for
-- earnings in my waiting period and is the waiting period waived; is my medical certificate enough, can the
-- Commission make me be examined, what proof of pregnancy must I give; how are the remaining weeks divided; my
-- work-sharing benefits; may I be paid after leaving under a work-force reduction process; days of disentitlement
-- for a part-time job lost to a stoppage; am I disentitled in an institution or outside Canada and for how many
-- weeks may I be paid there; what will my employer tell the Commission; can what I owe be written off, does
-- interest run on it, can a deduction be made from my benefits.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes plain inputs -- yes/no, numbers, dates and the modules' own choices -- one for
-- each fact the person can state, each with an @desc worded as the person would be asked. The records and lists the
-- layer-1 modules expect (the facts about an income, a list of weekly amounts) are built inside each question, in its
-- WHERE, from those answers, and the SAME layer-1 rule is then called; no rule is restated here. Where a rule needs
-- a list the person cannot sensibly state (the survival probabilities of reg 36(17)), the question takes the
-- result of that list instead (the Commission's value B), and says so.
--
-- JUDGMENTS LEFT TO THE COMMISSION are asked as facts about what the Commission has decided ("Has the Commission
-- determined a value ...?"), never guessed. The Commission's powers (reg 40(2), 40(6), 55.2, 56, 56.1(8)) are asked
-- as "could the Commission ...?": the answer says whether the conditions of the power are met, not whether it is used.
--
-- Where the text leaves a date to its commencement (reg 39.1 and reg 56.1), the question asks for that date: it is
-- not in the text.
--
-- The employer, the Commission and the Minister have no seat here: they appear only as the other party of a relation
-- the person holds (see NOTES.md, Jural relations).

§ `Employment Insurance Regulations 35 to 57 -- the questions of a person who has lost work or cannot work`

-- Small helpers that turn a plain yes/no answer into one fact of a list, for the questions that ask many facts.
GIVEN holds IS A BOOLEAN
      fact IS AN `er3 Fact about the income received`
GIVETH A LIST OF `er3 Fact about the income received`
`the seat's income fact for` holds `if the answer is yes` fact MEANS
    IF holds THEN LIST fact ELSE EMPTY

GIVEN holds IS A BOOLEAN
      fact IS AN `er3 Fact about earnings to be allocated`
GIVETH A LIST OF `er3 Fact about earnings to be allocated`
`the seat's earnings fact for` holds `if the answer is yes` fact MEANS
    IF holds THEN LIST fact ELSE EMPTY

-- The nth amount of a list of weekly amounts, counting the first week as week 1: NOTHING for a week beyond the last.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      amounts IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the seat's amount on week number` n `of` amounts MEANS
    IF n LESS THAN 1 OR n GREATER THAN (count amounts)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (at amounts (n MINUS 1))

§ `Regulation 35 -- does what I received count as earnings, and what is it worth`
-- Arises only for a person who received, or will receive, money or benefits from work, a business, a plan or a pension while claiming or about to claim: ask 'Did you receive any money or other benefit for work or from a plan or pension?'.

-- The definitions of reg 35(1) first: whether what a person receives is income from an employment, and whether a
-- payment is a pension. They decide what the person would ask: "does this payment count?"
@export Is what I receive income from an employment, within the meaning of regulation 35(1)?
GIVEN `I work under a contract of employment, whether insurable or not` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you work, or did you work, under an express or implied contract of service or other contract of employment (whether or not the work is insurable)?
      `I am self-employed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the income from your own business or self-employment, on your own account or in a partnership or co-adventure?
      `I hold an office as defined in the Canada Pension Plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the income from holding an office as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Canada Pension Plan?
      `what I receive is money` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is what you receive money (pecuniary income)?
      `what I receive is not money` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is what you receive something other than money, such as board, lodging or goods (non-pecuniary income)?
      `it comes from an employer, a trustee in bankruptcy or another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you receive it, or will you receive it, from an employer, from a trustee in bankruptcy or from anyone else?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is what I receive income from an employment` IF
        `reg 35(1) employment` `I work under a contract of employment, whether insurable or not` `I am self-employed` `I hold an office as defined in the Canada Pension Plan`
    AND `reg 35(1) income` `what I receive is money` `what I receive is not money` `it comes from an employer, a trustee in bankruptcy or another person`

@export Is what I receive a pension, within the meaning of regulation 35(1)?
GIVEN `it is a retirement pension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a retirement pension?
      `it arises out of my employment or my service in the armed forces or a police force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it arise out of employment, or out of service in any armed forces or in a police force?
      `it is paid under the Canada Pension Plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it paid under the Canada Pension Plan?
      `it is paid under a provincial pension plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it paid under a provincial pension plan?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is what I get a pension` IF
    `reg 35(1) pension` `it is a retirement pension` `it arises out of my employment or my service in the armed forces or a police force` `it is paid under the Canada Pension Plan` `it is paid under a provincial pension plan`

-- reg 35(2) to (7): is this payment earnings, for the purpose I ask about? The purpose is a choice of the module's
-- (an interruption of earnings under reg 14(2), under reg 14 otherwise, the deduction from benefits, or ss 45 and 46).
@export Does the income I received count as earnings, for the purpose I ask about (regulation 35)?
GIVEN purpose IS A `er3 Purpose of the determination of earnings` @desc For which purpose do you ask: whether an interruption of earnings has occurred under subsection 14(2) of the Regulations, or under section 14 otherwise, or how much is deducted from your benefits, or for sections 45 and 46 of the Act?
      `it arises out of my employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the income arise out of your employment (a job, self-employment or an office)?
      `it is paid from the property of my bankrupt employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it wages, benefits or other remuneration paid from the proceeds of the property of your bankrupt employer?
      `it is a workers' compensation payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a workers' compensation payment you have received or will receive?
      `it is a lump sum or pension in full and final settlement of a workers' compensation claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a lump sum or pension paid in full and final settlement of a claim for workers' compensation payments?
      `it is a disability pension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a disability pension?
      `it is paid under a sickness or disability wage-loss insurance plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it paid under a sickness or disability wage-loss indemnity plan?
      `that plan is not a group plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that plan one that regulation 35(8) says is not a group plan (see the question about group plans)?
      `it is paid under a paid sick, maternity or adoption leave plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it paid under a paid sick, maternity or adoption leave plan?
      `it is paid under a leave plan for the care of my child or children` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it paid under a leave plan for the care of a new-born or adopted child or children?
      `it is paid under a leave plan for the care or support of a family member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it paid under a leave plan for the care or support of a family member?
      `it is paid under a leave plan for the care or support of a critically ill child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it paid under a leave plan for the care or support of a critically ill child?
      `it is paid under a leave plan for the care or support of a critically ill adult` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it paid under a leave plan for the care or support of a critically ill adult?
      `it is paid by a provincial motor vehicle accident insurance plan for loss of income due to injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it paid by a motor vehicle accident insurance plan provided under a provincial law, for the actual or presumed loss of income from employment due to injury?
      `the benefits under the Act are not counted by that motor vehicle plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does that plan leave out of its calculation the benefits you get under the Employment Insurance Act?
      `it is paid on account of or in place of a pension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it money paid, periodically or in a lump sum, on account of or in place of a pension?
      `it is a provincial indemnity for stopping work because continuing it entailed physical dangers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an indemnity under a provincial law because you stopped working as continuing entailed physical dangers for you, your unborn child or the child you are breast-feeding?
      `the benefits under the Act are not counted by that provincial law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does that provincial law leave out of its calculation the benefits you get under the Employment Insurance Act?
      `I have since accumulated the hours required for benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc After the week in which you were injured, did you accumulate the number of hours of insurable employment that section 7 or 7.1 of the Act requires?
      `I am self-employed and was injured before the section 152.08 period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a self-employed person who was injured before the beginning of the period referred to in section 152.08 of the Act?
      `it is paid by reason of my lay-off or separation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it paid or payable by reason of a lay-off or separation from an employment?
      `it is an allowance that would not be deducted under section 16(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an allowance that would not be deducted from your benefits by virtue of subsection 16(1) of the Act?
      `it is a relief grant in cash or in kind` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a relief grant in cash or in kind?
      `it is a retroactive increase in wages or salary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a retroactive increase in wages or salary?
      `I am a self-employed person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a self-employed person?
      `the pension moneys became payable before the section 152.08 period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are self-employed: did the pension moneys become payable before the beginning of the period referred to in section 152.08 of the Act?
      `the hours were accumulated after the pension moneys became payable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are not self-employed: were the hours of insurable employment required for your benefit period accumulated after the pension moneys became payable and during the period for which you received them?
      `it is employment income excluded under subsection 6(16) of the Income Tax Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it employment income excluded from income by subsection 6(16) of the Income Tax Act?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the income I received count as earnings` IF
    `reg 35 the income is earnings to be taken into account for the purpose` `my income facts` purpose
    WHERE
        `my income facts` MEANS concat (LIST
            (`the seat's income fact for` `it arises out of my employment` `if the answer is yes` `er3 income: arising out of any employment`),
            (`the seat's income fact for` `it is paid from the property of my bankrupt employer` `if the answer is yes` `er3 income: payable in respect of wages, benefits or other remuneration from the proceeds realized from the property of a bankrupt employer`),
            (`the seat's income fact for` `it is a workers' compensation payment` `if the answer is yes` `er3 income: a workers' compensation payment received or to be received`),
            (`the seat's income fact for` `it is a lump sum or pension in full and final settlement of a workers' compensation claim` `if the answer is yes` `er3 income: a lump sum or pension paid in full and final settlement of a claim made for workers' compensation payments`),
            (`the seat's income fact for` `it is a disability pension` `if the answer is yes` `er3 income: a disability pension`),
            (`the seat's income fact for` `it is paid under a sickness or disability wage-loss insurance plan` `if the answer is yes` `er3 income: a payment under a sickness or disability wage-loss indemnity plan`),
            (`the seat's income fact for` `that plan is not a group plan` `if the answer is yes` `er3 income: that plan is not a group plan under subsection (8)`),
            (`the seat's income fact for` `it is paid under a paid sick, maternity or adoption leave plan` `if the answer is yes` `er3 income: a payment under a paid sick, maternity or adoption leave plan`),
            (`the seat's income fact for` `it is paid under a leave plan for the care of my child or children` `if the answer is yes` `er3 income: a payment under a leave plan for the care of a child or children referred to in subsection 23(1) or 152.05(1) of the Act`),
            (`the seat's income fact for` `it is paid under a leave plan for the care or support of a family member` `if the answer is yes` `er3 income: a payment under a leave plan for the care or support of a family member referred to in subsection 23.1(2) or 152.06(1) of the Act`),
            (`the seat's income fact for` `it is paid under a leave plan for the care or support of a critically ill child` `if the answer is yes` `er3 income: a payment under a leave plan for the care or support of a critically ill child`),
            (`the seat's income fact for` `it is paid under a leave plan for the care or support of a critically ill adult` `if the answer is yes` `er3 income: a payment under a leave plan for the care or support of a critically ill adult`),
            (`the seat's income fact for` `it is paid by a provincial motor vehicle accident insurance plan for loss of income due to injury` `if the answer is yes` `er3 income: a payment from a motor vehicle accident insurance plan provided under a provincial law in respect of the actual or presumed loss of income from employment due to injury`),
            (`the seat's income fact for` `the benefits under the Act are not counted by that motor vehicle plan` `if the answer is yes` `er3 income: the benefits under the Act are not taken into account in determining the amount received from that motor vehicle plan`),
            (`the seat's income fact for` `it is paid on account of or in place of a pension` `if the answer is yes` `er3 income: moneys paid or payable on account of or in lieu of a pension`),
            (`the seat's income fact for` `it is a provincial indemnity for stopping work because continuing it entailed physical dangers` `if the answer is yes` `er3 income: an indemnity payment under a provincial law because the claimant ceased to work as continuation of work entailed physical dangers`),
            (`the seat's income fact for` `the benefits under the Act are not counted by that provincial law` `if the answer is yes` `er3 income: the benefits under the Act are not taken into account in determining the amount received under that provincial law`),
            (`the seat's income fact for` `I have since accumulated the hours required for benefits` `if the answer is yes` `er3 income: after the week of the injury the claimant accumulated the hours of insurable employment required by section 7 or 7.1 of the Act`),
            (`the seat's income fact for` `I am self-employed and was injured before the section 152.08 period` `if the answer is yes` `er3 income: the claimant is a self-employed person who sustained the injury before the beginning of the period referred to in section 152.08 of the Act`),
            (`the seat's income fact for` `it is paid by reason of my lay-off or separation` `if the answer is yes` `er3 income: paid or payable by reason of a lay-off or separation from an employment`),
            (`the seat's income fact for` `it is an allowance that would not be deducted under section 16(1)` `if the answer is yes` `er3 income: an allowance that would not be deducted from benefits by virtue of subsection 16(1) of the Act`),
            (`the seat's income fact for` `it is a relief grant in cash or in kind` `if the answer is yes` `er3 income: relief grants in cash or in kind`),
            (`the seat's income fact for` `it is a retroactive increase in wages or salary` `if the answer is yes` `er3 income: a retroactive increase in wages or salary`),
            (`the seat's income fact for` `I am a self-employed person` `if the answer is yes` `er3 income: the claimant is a self-employed person`),
            (`the seat's income fact for` `the pension moneys became payable before the section 152.08 period` `if the answer is yes` `er3 income: the moneys became payable before the beginning of the period referred to in section 152.08 of the Act`),
            (`the seat's income fact for` `the hours were accumulated after the pension moneys became payable` `if the answer is yes` `er3 income: the hours of insurable employment required by section 7 or 7.1 of the Act for the benefit period were accumulated after the moneys became payable and during the period in respect of which they were received`),
            (`the seat's income fact for` `it is employment income excluded under subsection 6(16) of the Income Tax Act` `if the answer is yes` `er3 income: employment income excluded as income under subsection 6(16) of the Income Tax Act`))

-- reg 35(8) and (9): is my sickness or disability wage-loss insurance plan treated as NOT a group plan?
@export Is my wage-loss insurance plan treated as not a group plan, under regulation 35(8) and (9)?
GIVEN `the plan is related to a group of persons who are all employed by one employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the plan related to a group of persons who are all employed by the same employer?
      `the plan is financed in whole or in part by an employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the plan financed in whole or in part by an employer?
      `I bought the plan voluntarily` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you buy the plan voluntarily, as the person taking part in it?
      `my benefits would stay equivalent if I changed employer within my occupation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you became employed by another employer in the same occupation, would the benefits you are entitled to under the plan stay equivalent?
      `my premium would stay equivalent if I changed employer within my occupation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you became employed by another employer in the same occupation, would the rate of premium you pay stay equivalent?
      `the plan provides constant benefits while permitting deductions for income from other sources` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the plan provide constant benefits while permitting deductions for income from other sources, where that applies?
      `the plan's premium rates depend on the experience of that group` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the plan's rates of premium depend on the experience of a group of persons who are all employed by the same employer?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my wage-loss insurance plan treated as not a group plan` IF
    `reg 35(8) a sickness or disability wage-loss indemnity plan is not a group plan` `the plan is related to a group of persons who are all employed by one employer` `the plan is financed in whole or in part by an employer` `I bought the plan voluntarily` (`reg 35(9) portable` `my benefits would stay equivalent if I changed employer within my occupation` `my premium would stay equivalent if I changed employer within my occupation`) `the plan provides constant benefits while permitting deductions for income from other sources` `the plan's premium rates depend on the experience of that group`

-- reg 35(10) to (15): what the income is worth, with the value of board, living quarters and other benefits.
@export How much of my income from my work or business counts, including the value of the board, living quarters and other benefits I receive (regulation 35(10) to (15))?
GIVEN kind IS A `er3 Kind of claimant for the value of income` @desc Are you not self-employed, self-employed in farming, or self-employed in something other than farming?
      `the income I received` IS A NUMBER @desc If you are not self-employed: how much income did you receive, in dollars?
      `my expenses for the direct purpose of earning it` IS A NUMBER @desc If you are not self-employed: how much did you spend for the direct purpose of earning that income, in dollars?
      `the value of the consideration I supplied` IS A NUMBER @desc If you are not self-employed: what is the value of any consideration you supplied, in dollars?
      `my gross income from self-employment, without farming subsidies` IS A NUMBER @desc If you are self-employed: what was your gross income from the self-employment, not counting farming subsidies, in dollars?
      `my farming subsidies` IS A NUMBER @desc If you are self-employed in farming: how much did you receive in farming subsidies under any federal or provincial program, in dollars?
      `my operating expenses other than capital expenditures` IS A NUMBER @desc If you are self-employed: what were your operating expenses, other than capital expenditures, in dollars?
      `I receive board, living quarters or other benefits from my employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you receive board, living quarters or other benefits from your employer for your employment?
      `my employer and I have fixed a value for them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you and your employer agreed on a value for those benefits?
      `the value we fixed` IS A NUMBER @desc What value did you agree on, in dollars? (0 if none)
      `that value is reasonable in the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that value reasonable in the circumstances?
      `the Commission has determined a value` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Commission determined a value for those benefits, based on their monetary value?
      `the value the Commission determined` IS A NUMBER @desc What value did the Commission determine, in dollars? (0 if none yet)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of my income from my work or business counts` IS
    `reg 35(10) the income taken into account, with the value of board, living quarters and other benefits`
        (`reg 35(10)(a) to (c) the income from the employment` kind `the income I received` `my expenses for the direct purpose of earning it` `the value of the consideration I supplied` `my gross income from self-employment, without farming subsidies` `my farming subsidies` `my operating expenses other than capital expenditures`)
        `the value of my benefits in kind`
    WHERE
        `the value of my benefits in kind` MEANS
            IF `I receive board, living quarters or other benefits from my employer`
            THEN `reg 35(11) and (12) the value of the benefits referred to in paragraph (10)(d)` `my employer and I have fixed a value for them` `the value we fixed` `that value is reasonable in the circumstances` (IF `the Commission has determined a value` THEN JUST `the value the Commission determined` ELSE NOTHING)
            ELSE JUST 0

@export What is the value of my living quarters, including heat, light, telephone and other benefits (regulation 35(13) and (14))?
GIVEN `the value of the rooms or other living accommodation` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of the rooms or other living accommodation, in dollars?
      `the value of heat, light, telephone or other benefits included with them` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of any heat, light, telephone or other benefits included with the living quarters, in dollars?
      `the Commission has determined the value` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Commission determined the value of the living quarters?
      `the rental value of similar living quarters in the same vicinity or district` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the rental value of similar living quarters in the same vicinity or district, in dollars? (needed only if the Commission determined the value)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the value of my living quarters` IS
    IF `the Commission has determined the value`
    THEN `reg 35(14) the value of living quarters determined by the Commission` `the rental value of similar living quarters in the same vicinity or district`
    ELSE `reg 35(13) the value of living quarters` `the value of the rooms or other living accommodation` `the value of heat, light, telephone or other benefits included with them`

@export What value is added to my income for remuneration that is not money and is not board or living quarters (regulation 35(15))?
GIVEN `my remuneration is not money or only partly money` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your remuneration not in money, or only partly in money?
      `part of it is something other than living quarters and board from my employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does all or part of the non-money remuneration consist of something other than living quarters and board furnished by your employer?
      `the value of that other thing` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of that other consideration, in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What value is added to my income for other remuneration that is not money` IS
    `reg 35(15) the value of other non-pecuniary remuneration to be included in the income` `my remuneration is not money or only partly money` `part of it is something other than living quarters and board from my employer` `the value of that other thing`

@export Is where I live "living quarters" within the meaning of regulation 35(16)?
GIVEN `it is rooms` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it rooms?
      `it is other living accommodation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it any other living accommodation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is where I live living quarters` IF
    `reg 35(16) living quarters` `it is rooms` `it is other living accommodation`

§ `Regulation 36 -- to which weeks is the money put, and how much goes on each`
-- Arises only for a person whose money counts as earnings under regulation 35: ask 'Did money you received count as earnings?'.

@export Is the money I received put on weeks at all (regulation 36(1) and (2))?
GIVEN `it counts as earnings under regulation 35` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the money count as earnings under regulation 35 (see the question about earnings)?
      `it did not count as earnings in those weeks` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it fail to count as earnings, or fail to be taken into account as earnings, in the weeks concerned?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the money I received put on weeks at all` IF
    `reg 36(1) and (2) the earnings are allocated to weeks` `it counts as earnings under regulation 35` (`the seat's earnings fact for` `it did not count as earnings in those weeks` `if the answer is yes` `er3 earnings: they did not constitute earnings, or were not taken into account as earnings, under section 35`)

-- reg 36(2) to (19): the manner in which the earnings are allocated, by the kind of earnings.
@export To which weeks is the money I received allocated (regulation 36)?
GIVEN `it did not count as earnings in those weeks` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it fail to count as earnings, or fail to be taken into account as earnings, in the weeks concerned?
      `it is paid under my contract of employment for the services I performed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it payable under your contract of employment for the performance of services?
      `it is paid under my contract of employment without services` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it payable under your contract of employment without the performance of services?
      `it is paid to me for returning to or beginning work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it payable by an employer in consideration of your returning to or beginning work?
      `I am self-employed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you self-employed?
      `it is from profits or commissions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it from your participation in profits or commissions?
      `it arises from services I performed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it arise from your performing services?
      `it arises from a transaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it arise from a transaction?
      `I am self-employed in farming` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you self-employed in farming?
      `it was received as a subsidy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you receive it in the form of a subsidy?
      `it is vacation pay not paid because of a lay-off or separation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it vacation pay paid or payable for a reason other than a lay-off or separation?
      `it is for a specific vacation period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is vacation pay: is it paid or payable for a specific vacation period or periods?
      `it is paid because of my lay-off or separation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it paid or payable by reason of a lay-off or separation from an employment?
      `it is paid under a labour arbitration award or tribunal judgment or a settlement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it paid under a labour arbitration award or a tribunal's judgment, or as a settlement of an issue that might have been decided that way?
      `it is awarded for specific weeks after a finding that discipline was warranted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it awarded in respect of specific weeks as a result of a finding or admission that disciplinary action was warranted?
      `it is sick, maternity, adoption or child care leave pay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a payment in respect of sick leave, maternity leave or adoption leave or leave for the care of a child or children?
      `it is paid under a group sickness or disability wage-loss plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a payment under a group sickness or disability wage-loss indemnity plan?
      `it is a payment of a kind described in regulation 35(2)(d) or (f)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a payment referred to in paragraph 35(2)(d) or (f) (a motor vehicle plan or a provincial indemnity)?
      `it is a workers' compensation payment, not a final settlement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a workers' compensation payment, other than a lump sum or pension paid in full and final settlement?
      `it is for the care or support of a family member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a payment in respect of the care or support of a family member?
      `it is for the care or support of a critically ill child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a payment in respect of the care or support of a critically ill child?
      `it is for the care or support of a critically ill adult` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a payment in respect of the care or support of a critically ill adult?
      `it is pay for a holiday or non-working day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a payment in respect of a holiday or non-working day observed as such by law, custom or agreement?
      `it is pay for a day next to a holiday at my employer's establishment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a payment in respect of a holiday or non-working day immediately before or after one that occurs at the establishment of your employer or former employer?
      `it is moneys on account of or in place of a pension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it money paid on account of or in place of a pension (regulation 35(2)(e))?
      `it is paid periodically` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it paid or payable on a periodic basis?
      `it is paid in a lump sum` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it paid or payable in a lump sum?
      `it is a government re-employment supplement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it payable under a government program intended to encourage re-employment, as a supplement to earnings from a contract of employment?
GIVETH A MAYBE `er3 Manner of allocation`
DECIDE `To which weeks is the money I received allocated` IS
    `reg 36 the manner of allocation that governs` `my earnings facts`
    WHERE
        `my earnings facts` MEANS concat (LIST
            (`the seat's earnings fact for` `it did not count as earnings in those weeks` `if the answer is yes` `er3 earnings: they did not constitute earnings, or were not taken into account as earnings, under section 35`),
            (`the seat's earnings fact for` `it is paid under my contract of employment for the services I performed` `if the answer is yes` `er3 earnings: payable under a contract of employment for the performance of services`),
            (`the seat's earnings fact for` `it is paid under my contract of employment without services` `if the answer is yes` `er3 earnings: payable under a contract of employment without the performance of services`),
            (`the seat's earnings fact for` `it is paid to me for returning to or beginning work` `if the answer is yes` `er3 earnings: payable by an employer in consideration of the claimant returning to or beginning work`),
            (`the seat's earnings fact for` `I am self-employed` `if the answer is yes` `er3 earnings: the claimant is self-employed`),
            (`the seat's earnings fact for` `it is from profits or commissions` `if the answer is yes` `er3 earnings: from participation in profits or commissions`),
            (`the seat's earnings fact for` `it arises from services I performed` `if the answer is yes` `er3 earnings: they arise from the performance of services`),
            (`the seat's earnings fact for` `it arises from a transaction` `if the answer is yes` `er3 earnings: they arise from a transaction`),
            (`the seat's earnings fact for` `I am self-employed in farming` `if the answer is yes` `er3 earnings: the claimant is self-employed in farming`),
            (`the seat's earnings fact for` `it was received as a subsidy` `if the answer is yes` `er3 earnings: received in the form of a subsidy`),
            (`the seat's earnings fact for` `it is vacation pay not paid because of a lay-off or separation` `if the answer is yes` `er3 earnings: vacation pay paid or payable for a reason other than a lay-off or separation`),
            (`the seat's earnings fact for` `it is for a specific vacation period` `if the answer is yes` `er3 earnings: the vacation pay is paid or payable for a specific vacation period or periods`),
            (`the seat's earnings fact for` `it is paid because of my lay-off or separation` `if the answer is yes` `er3 earnings: paid or payable by reason of a lay-off or separation from an employment`),
            (`the seat's earnings fact for` `it is paid under a labour arbitration award or tribunal judgment or a settlement` `if the answer is yes` `er3 earnings: paid or payable under a labour arbitration award or tribunal judgment, or as a settlement of an issue that might have been so determined`),
            (`the seat's earnings fact for` `it is awarded for specific weeks after a finding that discipline was warranted` `if the answer is yes` `er3 earnings: awarded in respect of specific weeks as a result of a finding or admission that disciplinary action was warranted`),
            (`the seat's earnings fact for` `it is sick, maternity, adoption or child care leave pay` `if the answer is yes` `er3 earnings: a payment in respect of sick leave, maternity leave or adoption leave or leave for the care of a child or children`),
            (`the seat's earnings fact for` `it is paid under a group sickness or disability wage-loss plan` `if the answer is yes` `er3 earnings: a payment under a group sickness or disability wage-loss indemnity plan`),
            (`the seat's earnings fact for` `it is a payment of a kind described in regulation 35(2)(d) or (f)` `if the answer is yes` `er3 earnings: a payment referred to in paragraph 35(2)(d) or (f)`),
            (`the seat's earnings fact for` `it is a workers' compensation payment, not a final settlement` `if the answer is yes` `er3 earnings: workers' compensation payments, other than a lump sum or pension paid in full and final settlement`),
            (`the seat's earnings fact for` `it is for the care or support of a family member` `if the answer is yes` `er3 earnings: a payment in respect of the care or support of a family member`),
            (`the seat's earnings fact for` `it is for the care or support of a critically ill child` `if the answer is yes` `er3 earnings: a payment in respect of the care or support of a critically ill child`),
            (`the seat's earnings fact for` `it is for the care or support of a critically ill adult` `if the answer is yes` `er3 earnings: a payment in respect of the care or support of a critically ill adult`),
            (`the seat's earnings fact for` `it is pay for a holiday or non-working day` `if the answer is yes` `er3 earnings: a payment in respect of a holiday or non-working day observed as such by law, custom or agreement`),
            (`the seat's earnings fact for` `it is pay for a day next to a holiday at my employer's establishment` `if the answer is yes` `er3 earnings: a payment in respect of a holiday or non-working day immediately preceding or following one that occurs at the establishment of the employer or former employer`),
            (`the seat's earnings fact for` `it is moneys on account of or in place of a pension` `if the answer is yes` `er3 earnings: the moneys referred to in paragraph 35(2)(e)`),
            (`the seat's earnings fact for` `it is paid periodically` `if the answer is yes` `er3 earnings: paid or payable on a periodic basis`),
            (`the seat's earnings fact for` `it is paid in a lump sum` `if the answer is yes` `er3 earnings: paid or payable in a lump sum`),
            (`the seat's earnings fact for` `it is a government re-employment supplement` `if the answer is yes` `er3 earnings: payable under a government program intended to encourage re-employment, as a supplement to earnings arising from a contract of employment`))

-- reg 36(3): pay for a period that does not coincide with a week.
@export How much of my pay for a period that is not a week is put on a given week (regulation 36(3))?
GIVEN `my pay for the period` IS A NUMBER @desc How much are you paid for the period, in dollars?
      `the first day of the period` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the period (YYYY-MM-DD)?
      `the last day of the period` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the period (YYYY-MM-DD)?
      `the Sunday that begins the week I ask about` IS A DATE @desc Which week do you ask about? Give the Sunday that begins it (YYYY-MM-DD).
      `the days I worked in that week` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days did you work in that week?
      `the days I worked in the whole period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days did you work in the whole period?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of my pay for a period that is not a week is put on a given week` IS
    `reg 36(3) the earnings allocated to a week` `my pay for the period` (`Period of days` OF `the first day of the period`, `the last day of the period`) `the Sunday that begins the week I ask about` `the days I worked in that week` `the days I worked in the whole period`

-- reg 36(6.1): earnings of a self-employed person, or from profits or commissions, that arise from a transaction.
@export Where are the earnings from my transaction allocated (regulation 36(6.1))?
GIVEN `the earnings from transactions occurring in the week` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total of the earnings that arise from transactions occurring in the week, in dollars?
      `the maximum yearly insurable earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the maximum yearly insurable earnings under section 4 of the Act for the year, in dollars? (the published figure; the Regulations divide it by 52)
      `I did the work that gave rise to the transaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was work performed that gave rise to the transaction?
      `I can show the work was done in more than one week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you demonstrate that the work that gave rise to the transaction was done in more than one week?
GIVETH A `er3 Allocation of earnings from a transaction`
DECIDE `Where are the earnings from my transaction allocated` IS
    `reg 36(6.1) where the earnings from a transaction are allocated` `the earnings from transactions occurring in the week` `the maximum yearly insurable earnings` `I did the work that gave rise to the transaction` `I can show the work was done in more than one week`

@export How much of the earnings from my transaction goes on a week, in proportion to the work I did in it (regulation 36(6.1))?
GIVEN `the earnings from the transaction` IS A NUMBER @desc How much did the transaction earn, in dollars?
      `the work I did in the week` IS A NUMBER @desc How much work did you do in that week (hours, days or any one unit)?
      `the work I did in all the weeks` IS A NUMBER @desc How much work did you do in all the weeks together (the same unit)?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of the earnings from my transaction goes on a week` IS
    `reg 36(6.1) the share of the earnings allocated to a week in proportion to the work` `the earnings from the transaction` `the work I did in the week` `the work I did in all the weeks`

@export How much goes on each week when my earnings are spread equally over the weeks in which I earned them (regulation 36(6.2))?
GIVEN `my earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc How much are the earnings, in dollars?
      `the number of weeks falling within the period in which I earned them` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks fall within the period in which you earned them?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much goes on each week when my earnings are spread equally` IS
    `reg 36(6.2) the equal share allocated to each week` `my earnings` `the number of weeks falling within the period in which I earned them`

-- reg 36(7)(b), 36(13), 36(19)(b): the week a payment is put on when it goes to the week of a day.
@export Which week is my farming subsidy put on (regulation 36(7)(b))?
GIVEN `the day the subsidy was paid` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the subsidy paid (YYYY-MM-DD)?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Which week is my farming subsidy put on` IS
    `reg 36(7)(b) the week to which a farming subsidy is allocated` `the day the subsidy was paid`

@export Which week is my pay for a holiday or non-working day put on (regulation 36(13))?
GIVEN `the day of the holiday or non-working day` IS A DATE @desc What is the day of the holiday or non-working day (YYYY-MM-DD)?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Which week is my pay for a holiday or non-working day put on` IS
    `reg 36(13) the week to which a payment for a holiday or non-working day is allocated` `the day of the holiday or non-working day`

@export Which week are my earnings from a transaction put on when they go to the week of the transaction (regulation 36(19)(b))?
GIVEN `the day the transaction occurs` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the transaction occur (YYYY-MM-DD)?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Which week are my earnings from a transaction put on` IS
    `reg 36(19)(b) the week to which earnings from a transaction are allocated` `the day the transaction occurs`

-- reg 36(8): vacation pay.
@export How much of my vacation pay for a specific vacation goes on a given week of it (regulation 36(8)(a))?
GIVEN `my vacation pay` IS A NUMBER @desc How much vacation pay are you paid, in dollars?
      `my normal weekly earnings from that employment` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your normal weekly earnings from that employment, in dollars?
      `my other earnings from that employment on each week of the vacation` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc What other earnings did you have from that employment on each week of the vacation, in order, in dollars? (one number per week)
      `the number of the week I ask about` IS A NUMBER @desc Which week of the vacation do you ask about (1 for the first)?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of my vacation pay for a specific vacation goes on a given week` IS
    `the seat's amount on week number` `the number of the week I ask about` `of` (`reg 36(8)(a) the amounts put on the weeks of the vacation period or periods` `my vacation pay` `my normal weekly earnings from that employment` `my other earnings from that employment on each week of the vacation`)

@export How much of my vacation pay does not fit in the weeks of my vacation (regulation 36(8)(a))?
GIVEN `my vacation pay` IS A NUMBER @desc How much vacation pay are you paid, in dollars?
      `my normal weekly earnings from that employment` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your normal weekly earnings from that employment, in dollars?
      `my other earnings from that employment on each week of the vacation` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc What other earnings did you have from that employment on each week of the vacation, in order, in dollars? (one number per week)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of my vacation pay does not fit in the weeks of my vacation` IS
    `reg 36(8)(a) the vacation pay that does not fit on the weeks of the vacation period or periods` `my vacation pay` `my normal weekly earnings from that employment` `my other earnings from that employment on each week of the vacation`

@export How much of my vacation pay, paid otherwise than for a specific vacation, goes on a given week (regulation 36(8)(b))?
GIVEN `my vacation pay` IS A NUMBER @desc How much vacation pay are you paid, in dollars?
      `my normal weekly earnings from that employment` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your normal weekly earnings from that employment, in dollars?
      `the number of the week I ask about` IS A NUMBER @desc Which week do you ask about, counting from the first week for which the vacation pay is payable (1 for the first)?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of my vacation pay paid otherwise than for a specific vacation goes on a given week` IS
    `the seat's amount on week number` `the number of the week I ask about` `of` (`reg 36(8)(b) the amounts put on the weeks beginning with the first week for which the vacation pay is payable` `my vacation pay` `my normal weekly earnings from that employment`)

-- reg 36(9) to (11): lay-off or separation pay, and awards.
@export Over how many weeks is my lay-off or separation pay spread (regulation 36(9))?
GIVEN `my pay by reason of the lay-off or separation` IS A NUMBER @desc How much are you paid by reason of the lay-off or separation, in dollars?
      `my normal weekly earnings from that employment` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your normal weekly earnings from that employment, in dollars?
      `my other earnings from that employment on each week from the week of the lay-off` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc What other earnings did you have from that employment on each week from the week of the lay-off or separation, in order, in dollars? (one number per week; a week not listed has none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Over how many weeks is my lay-off or separation pay spread` IS
    count (`reg 36(9) the amounts put on the weeks beginning with the week of the lay-off or separation` `my pay by reason of the lay-off or separation` `my normal weekly earnings from that employment` `my other earnings from that employment on each week from the week of the lay-off`)

@export How much of my lay-off or separation pay goes on a given week (regulation 36(9))?
GIVEN `my pay by reason of the lay-off or separation` IS A NUMBER @desc How much are you paid by reason of the lay-off or separation, in dollars?
      `my normal weekly earnings from that employment` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your normal weekly earnings from that employment, in dollars?
      `my other earnings from that employment on each week from the week of the lay-off` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc What other earnings did you have from that employment on each week from the week of the lay-off or separation, in order, in dollars? (one number per week; a week not listed has none)
      `the number of the week I ask about` IS A NUMBER @desc Which week do you ask about, counting the week of the lay-off or separation as 1?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of my lay-off or separation pay goes on a given week` IS
    `the seat's amount on week number` `the number of the week I ask about` `of` (`reg 36(9) the amounts put on the weeks beginning with the week of the lay-off or separation` `my pay by reason of the lay-off or separation` `my normal weekly earnings from that employment` `my other earnings from that employment on each week from the week of the lay-off`)

@export How much of my lay-off or separation pay goes on a given week once more pay has come in (regulation 36(10))?
GIVEN `the pay already allocated` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of the lay-off or separation pay had already been allocated, in dollars?
      `the further pay` IS A NUMBER @desc How much further pay has been paid or is payable by reason of the same lay-off or separation, in dollars?
      `my normal weekly earnings from that employment` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your normal weekly earnings from that employment, in dollars?
      `my other earnings from that employment on each week from the week of the lay-off` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc What other earnings did you have from that employment on each week from the week of the lay-off or separation, in order, in dollars? (one number per week; a week not listed has none)
      `the number of the week I ask about` IS A NUMBER @desc Which week do you ask about, counting the week of the lay-off or separation as 1?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of my lay-off or separation pay goes on a given week once more pay has come in` IS
    `the seat's amount on week number` `the number of the week I ask about` `of` (`reg 36(10) the revised amounts put on the weeks beginning with the week of the lay-off or separation` `the pay already allocated` `the further pay` `my normal weekly earnings from that employment` `my other earnings from that employment on each week from the week of the lay-off`)

@export Does the spreading of my lay-off or separation pay not apply to me, because I was referred to a course (regulation 36(10.1) and (10.2))?
GIVEN `the first day of my benefit period` IS A DATE @desc On what day does your benefit period begin (YYYY-MM-DD)?
      `the number of the 10 years before in which I paid at least 30% of the maximum employee's premium` IS A NUMBER @desc In how many of the 10 years before your benefit period began did you contribute at least 30% of the maximum annual employee's premium?
      `the weeks of regular benefits paid to me in the 260 weeks before` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks of regular benefits did the Commission pay you in the 260 weeks before your benefit period began?
      `the first day of the weeks my lay-off pay is allocated to` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the period to which your lay-off pay is allocated under regulation 36(9) (YYYY-MM-DD)?
      `the last day of the weeks my lay-off pay is allocated to` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of that period (YYYY-MM-DD)?
      `the day I was notified of the allocation` IS A DATE @desc On what day were you notified of the allocation (YYYY-MM-DD)?
      `the day I was referred to a course` IS A DATE @desc On what day were you referred by the Commission, or an authority it designates, to a course or program of instruction or training (YYYY-MM-DD)?
      `the course is full-time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the course full-time?
      `the course lasts this many weeks` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks does the course last?
      `the course costs this many dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc How much does the course cost, in dollars?
      `my pay by reason of the lay-off or separation` IS A NUMBER @desc How much are you paid by reason of the lay-off or separation, in dollars?
      `I pay the whole cost of the course` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you assume the entire cost of the course?
      `the day the course begins` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the course begin (YYYY-MM-DD)?
      `a ground for ending my referral exists` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does any condition exist under which the Commission may terminate your referral (paragraph 27(1.1)(b) of the Act)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the spreading of my lay-off or separation pay not apply to me` IF
    NOT (`reg 36(9) the earnings are allocated under subsection (9), after subsections (10.1) and (10.2)` `the allocation does not apply by reason of subsection (10.1)` `a ground for ending my referral exists`)
    WHERE
        `the allocation does not apply by reason of subsection (10.1)` MEANS
            `reg 36(10.1) the allocation under subsection (9) does not apply` `the first day of my benefit period` `the number of the 10 years before in which I paid at least 30% of the maximum employee's premium` `the weeks of regular benefits paid to me in the 260 weeks before` (`Period of days` OF `the first day of the weeks my lay-off pay is allocated to`, `the last day of the weeks my lay-off pay is allocated to`) `the day I was notified of the allocation` `the day I was referred to a course` `the course is full-time` `the course lasts this many weeks` `the course costs this many dollars` `my pay by reason of the lay-off or separation` `I pay the whole cost of the course` `the day the course begins`

@export How much of the award or settlement I received for specific weeks goes on a given week (regulation 36(11))?
GIVEN `the earnings awarded` IS A NUMBER @desc How much was awarded, in dollars?
      `my normal weekly earnings from that employment` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your normal weekly earnings from that employment, in dollars?
      `my other earnings from that employment on each week from the first week awarded` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc What other earnings did you have from that employment on each week from the first week awarded, in order, in dollars? (one number per week; a week not listed has none)
      `the number of the week I ask about` IS A NUMBER @desc Which week do you ask about, counting the first week awarded as 1?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of my award or settlement for specific weeks goes on a given week` IS
    `the seat's amount on week number` `the number of the week I ask about` `of` (`reg 36(11) the amounts put on the consecutive weeks beginning with the first week awarded` `the earnings awarded` `my normal weekly earnings from that employment` `my other earnings from that employment on each week from the first week awarded`)

-- reg 36(15) to (17): a lump sum on account of a pension. The survival probabilities and the bond yield behind B are
-- not facts the person can state, so the question takes B, which the Commission calculates each year, as the input.
@export What weekly amount is my lump-sum pension payment treated as (regulation 36(15) to (17))?
GIVEN `the lump sum I was paid` IS A NUMBER @desc How much is the lump-sum payment, in dollars?
      `the value B calculated by the Commission` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the estimated actuarial present value B, as calculated each year in accordance with regulation 36(17)? (ask the Commission)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What weekly amount is my lump-sum pension payment treated as` IS
    `reg 36(17) the weekly amount A / B` `the lump sum I was paid` `the value B calculated by the Commission`

@export How much of my lump-sum pension payment goes on a given week (regulation 36(15))?
GIVEN `the lump sum I was paid` IS A NUMBER @desc How much is the lump-sum payment, in dollars?
      `the value B calculated by the Commission` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the estimated actuarial present value B, as calculated each year in accordance with regulation 36(17)? (ask the Commission)
      `the number of the week I ask about` IS A NUMBER @desc Which week do you ask about, counting the first week the lump sum is paid or payable as 1?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of my lump-sum pension payment goes on a given week` IS
    CONSIDER `reg 36(17) the weekly amount A / B` `the lump sum I was paid` `the value B calculated by the Commission`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST weekly THEN `the seat's amount on week number` `the number of the week I ask about` `of` (`reg 36(15) the amounts put on the weeks beginning with the first week the lump sum is paid or payable` `the lump sum I was paid` weekly)

-- reg 36(16): the pension moneys put on a week by (14) or (15) are not counted in allocating the rest.
@export How much of the earnings already on a week count when my other earnings are allocated (regulation 36(16))?
GIVEN `my other earnings on the week` IS A NUMBER @desc How much other earnings are already on the week, in dollars?
      `my pension moneys put on the week under subsection (14) or (15)` IS A NUMBER @desc How much pension money is on the week under regulation 36(14) or (15), in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of the earnings already on a week count when my other earnings are allocated` IS
    `reg 36(16) the earnings taken into account in allocating other earnings` (LIST (`er3 Earnings already on a week` OF `my other earnings on the week`, FALSE), (`er3 Earnings already on a week` OF `my pension moneys put on the week under subsection (14) or (15)`, TRUE))

§ `Regulations 37 and 38 -- my employer's plan, and the top-up of my leave pay`
-- Arises only for a person whose employer runs a plan that tops up or replaces pay (a supplemental unemployment benefit plan, or pay on a maternity, parental or care leave): ask 'Does your employer pay you anything while you are off work?' before showing the group.

@export Is my employer's plan a supplemental unemployment benefit plan (regulation 37(2))?
GIVEN `the plan identifies the group or groups of employees it covers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the plan identify the group or groups of employees it covers?
      `the plan covers periods of unemployment from a temporary stoppage of work, training, illness, injury or quarantine` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the plan cover any period of unemployment by reason of a temporary stoppage of work, training, illness, injury, quarantine or any combination of such reasons?
      `the plan requires employees to apply for and be in receipt of benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the plan require employees to apply for and be in receipt of Employment Insurance benefits in order to receive payments?
      `the plan pays an employee who is serving the waiting period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the plan provide for payments to an employee who is not in receipt of benefits because the employee is serving the waiting period?
      `the plan pays an employee with insufficient hours` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the plan provide for payments to an employee who is not in receipt of benefits because the employee has insufficient hours of insurable employment to qualify?
      `the plan pays an employee who has received all the benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the plan provide for payments to an employee who is not in receipt of benefits because the employee has received all the benefits to which they are entitled?
      `the plan pays an employee who is not in receipt of benefits for some other reason` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the plan provide for payments to an employee who is not in receipt of benefits for any other reason?
      `the plan keeps combined weekly payments within 95 per cent of normal weekly earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the plan require that the combined weekly payments from the plan and the portion of the weekly benefit rate from that employment not exceed 95 per cent of the employee's normal weekly earnings from that employment?
      `the plan is financed by the employer with separate accounts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the plan require that payments be financed by the employer and that the employer keep separate accounts for them?
      `on termination the remaining assets revert to the employer or are used for the plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the plan require that, on its termination, all remaining assets revert to the employer or be used for payments under the plan or its administrative costs?
      `the plan must be submitted to the Commission and changes notified within 30 days` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the plan require that it be submitted to the Commission before its effective date, and that written notice of any change be given to the Commission within 30 days after the change takes effect?
      `employees have no vested right except to payments in a specified period of unemployment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the plan provide that employees have no vested right to payments, except to payments during a period of unemployment specified in the plan?
      `guaranteed annual remuneration, deferred remuneration and severance pay are not changed by the plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the plan provide that payments in respect of guaranteed annual remuneration, deferred remuneration or severance pay benefits are not reduced or increased by payments under the plan?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my employer's plan a supplemental unemployment benefit plan` IF
    `reg 37(2) supplemental unemployment benefit plan` `the plan identifies the group or groups of employees it covers` `the plan covers periods of unemployment from a temporary stoppage of work, training, illness, injury or quarantine` (`reg 37(2)(c) the plan requires application for and receipt of benefits, with only the permitted exceptions` `the plan requires employees to apply for and be in receipt of benefits` `the reasons the plan pays an employee who is not in receipt of benefits`) `the plan keeps combined weekly payments within 95 per cent of normal weekly earnings` `the plan is financed by the employer with separate accounts` `on termination the remaining assets revert to the employer or are used for the plan` `the plan must be submitted to the Commission and changes notified within 30 days` `employees have no vested right except to payments in a specified period of unemployment` `guaranteed annual remuneration, deferred remuneration and severance pay are not changed by the plan`
    WHERE
        `the reasons the plan pays an employee who is not in receipt of benefits` MEANS concat (LIST
            (IF `the plan pays an employee who is serving the waiting period` THEN LIST `er3 reason: the employee is serving the waiting period` ELSE EMPTY),
            (IF `the plan pays an employee with insufficient hours` THEN LIST `er3 reason: the employee has insufficient hours of insurable employment to qualify for benefits` ELSE EMPTY),
            (IF `the plan pays an employee who has received all the benefits` THEN LIST `er3 reason: the employee has received all of the benefits to which the employee is entitled` ELSE EMPTY),
            (IF `the plan pays an employee who is not in receipt of benefits for some other reason` THEN LIST `er3 reason: some other reason` ELSE EMPTY))

@export Are the payments I receive from my employer's plan left out of my earnings (regulation 37(1))?
GIVEN `I receive the payments as an insured person under the plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you receive the payments as an insured person under the plan?
      `the plan is a supplemental unemployment benefit plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the plan a supplemental unemployment benefit plan (see the question about the plan)?
      purpose IS A `er3 Purpose of the determination of earnings` @desc For which purpose do you ask: whether an interruption of earnings has occurred under subsection 14(2) of the Regulations, or under section 14 otherwise, or how much is deducted from your benefits, or for sections 45 and 46 of the Act?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are the payments I receive from my employer's plan left out of my earnings` IF
    `reg 37(1) payments under a supplemental unemployment benefit plan are not earnings for the purpose` `I receive the payments as an insured person under the plan` `the plan is a supplemental unemployment benefit plan` purpose

@export What is the most my employer's plan may pay me for a week (regulation 37(2)(d))?
GIVEN `my normal weekly earnings from that employment` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your normal weekly earnings from that employment, in dollars?
      `the portion of my weekly benefit rate from that employment` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the portion of your weekly benefit rate that comes from that employment, in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most my employer's plan may pay me for a week` IS
    `reg 37(2)(d) the most the plan may pay for a week` `my normal weekly earnings from that employment` `the portion of my weekly benefit rate from that employment`

@export How much of the top-up I receive on my maternity, parental or care leave is left out of my earnings (regulation 38)?
GIVEN `the reason for my benefits` IS A `Reason for benefits` @desc Why are you claiming benefits: pregnancy, caring for a new-born or adopted child, care or support of a family member, care of a critically ill child or adult, an illness, injury or quarantine, or something else?
      `the payments I receive from my employer` IS A NUMBER @desc How much are you paid for the week by your employer, as an insured person, because of that reason, in dollars?
      `the part of them that reduces my sick leave, vacation, severance or other credits` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of that payment reduces your accumulated sick leave or vacation leave credits, severance pay or any other accumulated credits, in dollars?
      `my normal weekly earnings from that employment` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your normal weekly earnings from that employment, in dollars?
      `the portion of my weekly benefit rate from that employment` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the portion of your weekly benefit rate that comes from that employment, in dollars?
      `benefits are payable to me for that week for an illness, injury or quarantine` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are benefits payable to you for that week by reason of illness, injury or quarantine?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of the top-up I receive on my leave is left out of my earnings` IS
    `reg 38 the portion of the payments for the week that is excluded as earnings` (LIST `the reason for my benefits`) `the payments I receive from my employer` `the part of them that reduces my sick leave, vacation, severance or other credits` `my normal weekly earnings from that employment` `the portion of my weekly benefit rate from that employment` `benefits are payable to me for that week for an illness, injury or quarantine`

§ `Regulations 39 and 39.1 -- earnings in my waiting period, and my waiting period waived`
-- Arises only for a person who is serving, or has just served, the waiting period (39), or is an apprentice attending a required course (39.1): ask 'Are you serving your waiting period?' and 'Are you an apprentice attending a course you were referred to?'.

@export How much will be deducted from my benefits for earnings I had in my waiting period (regulation 39)?
GIVEN `the earnings I had in my waiting period that count` IS A NUMBER @desc How much did you earn in respect of periods in your waiting period, not counting the payments listed in the next question, in dollars?
      `the amounts I received in it from a wage-loss plan, workers' compensation, a 35(2)(f) indemnity or my employer's leave pay` IS A NUMBER @desc How much did you receive in respect of periods in your waiting period under a wage-loss indemnity plan for illness, injury, quarantine, pregnancy or care; under a workers' compensation plan; as an indemnity described in regulation 35(2)(f); or from your employer as sick, maternity, adoption or care leave pay, in dollars?
      `paragraph 19(3)(a) or 152.18(3)(a) of the Act applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does paragraph 19(3)(a) or 152.18(3)(a) of the Act (undeclared or misrepresented earnings) apply to those earnings?
      `the amount that paragraph requires to be deducted` IS A NUMBER @desc If it applies: what amount does that paragraph require to be deducted, in dollars? (0 if it does not apply)
      `my rate of weekly benefits` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your rate of weekly benefits, in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much will be deducted from my benefits for earnings I had in my waiting period` IS
    `reg 39 the amount deducted from the benefits payable for the first three weeks` `my amounts in the waiting period` `paragraph 19(3)(a) or 152.18(3)(a) of the Act applies` `the amount that paragraph requires to be deducted` `my rate of weekly benefits`
    WHERE
        `my amounts in the waiting period` MEANS LIST
            (`er3 Amount paid or payable in the waiting period` OF `the earnings I had in my waiting period that count`, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE),
            (`er3 Amount paid or payable in the waiting period` OF `the amounts I received in it from a wage-loss plan, workers' compensation, a 35(2)(f) indemnity or my employer's leave pay`, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE)

@export From how many weeks of my benefits is the deduction made (regulation 39(1))?
GIVEN `I had earnings in respect of a period in my waiting period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have earnings in respect of a period that falls in your waiting period?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `From how many weeks of my benefits is the deduction made` IS
    IF `I had earnings in respect of a period in my waiting period`
    THEN JUST `reg 39(1) the number of weeks of benefits from which the deduction is made`
    ELSE NOTHING

@export Is my waiting period waived because I am an apprentice (regulation 39.1)?
GIVEN `I am attending a required course of an apprenticeship program to which I was referred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you attending a course that is a required part of an apprenticeship program and to which you were referred under paragraph 25(1)(a) of the Act?
      `I stopped working because of the course` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you stopped working because you are attending that course?
      `I served a waiting period for a course of the same apprenticeship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you served a waiting period in respect of a course that is a required part of the same apprenticeship program?
      `the day I served that waiting period` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you serve that waiting period (YYYY-MM-DD)?
      `the day regulation 39.1 came into force` IS A DATE @desc On what day did regulation 39.1 come into force (YYYY-MM-DD)? (the text of the Regulations does not say; ask the Commission)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my waiting period waived because I am an apprentice` IF
    `reg 39.1 the waiting period is waived` `I am attending a required course of an apprenticeship program to which I was referred` `I stopped working because of the course` `I served a waiting period for a course of the same apprenticeship` `the day I served that waiting period` `the day regulation 39.1 came into force`

§ `Regulation 40 -- sickness`
-- Arises only for a person claiming because of illness, injury or quarantine: ask 'Are you unable to work because of illness, injury or quarantine?'.

@export Is my medical certificate enough to prove I cannot work because of illness, injury or quarantine (regulation 40(1))?
GIVEN `my certificate was completed by a medical doctor or other medical professional` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the certificate completed by a medical doctor or other medical professional?
      `it attests to my inability to work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it attest to your inability to work?
      `it states the probable duration of the illness, injury or quarantine` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state the probable duration of the illness, injury or quarantine?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my medical certificate enough to prove I cannot work` IF
    `reg 40(1) the medical certificate is the information and evidence required` `my certificate was completed by a medical doctor or other medical professional` `it attests to my inability to work` `it states the probable duration of the illness, injury or quarantine`

@export Can the Commission make me undergo a medical examination even though I gave a certificate (regulation 40(2))?
GIVEN `the Commission has directed me to undergo a medical examination` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Commission directed you to undergo a medical examination?
      `the time and place it directs are reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the time and place the Commission directs reasonable?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Commission make me undergo a medical examination` IF
    `reg 40(2) the claimant may be required to undergo a medical examination` `the Commission has directed me to undergo a medical examination` `the time and place it directs are reasonable`

@export How much will I be reimbursed for my travel and other expenses of the medical examination (regulation 40(3))?
GIVEN `the Commission required the examination` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the examination one that the Commission required of you under regulation 40(2)?
      `my travel and other expenses of the examination` IS A NUMBER @desc What were your travel and other expenses of the examination, in dollars?
      `the part of those expenses that is reasonable` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of those expenses is reasonable, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much will I be reimbursed for the medical examination` IS
    `reg 40(3) the amount the claimant is reimbursed for the examination` `the Commission required the examination` `my travel and other expenses of the examination` `the part of those expenses that is reasonable`

@export Does my illness, injury or quarantine count for the purposes of the Act (regulation 40(4))?
GIVEN `I have an illness, injury or quarantine` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have an illness, injury or quarantine?
      `it makes me incapable of doing the duties of my regular or usual employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it make you incapable of performing the duties of your regular or usual employment?
      `it makes me incapable of doing the duties of other suitable employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it make you incapable of performing the duties of other suitable employment?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my illness, injury or quarantine count` IF
    `reg 40(4) illness, injury or quarantine` `I have an illness, injury or quarantine` `it makes me incapable of doing the duties of my regular or usual employment` `it makes me incapable of doing the duties of other suitable employment`

@export Is my pregnancy that ended early treated as an illness (regulation 40(5))?
GIVEN `my pregnancy was terminated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your pregnancy terminated?
      `the weeks it had run when it ended` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks had the pregnancy run when it was terminated?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my pregnancy that ended early treated as an illness` IF
    `reg 40(5) a pregnancy terminated within the first 19 weeks is an illness` `my pregnancy was terminated` `the weeks it had run when it ended`

@export Could the Commission waive my waiting period because my employer pays me sick leave pay (regulation 40(6))?
GIVEN `I qualify for benefits by an interruption of earnings from illness, injury, quarantine, pregnancy or care` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you qualify to receive benefits in that benefit period by reason of an interruption of earnings described in regulation 14(2) or 14.01 (illness, injury, quarantine, pregnancy, or the need to care for a child or family member)?
      `my employer or former employer pays me sick leave pay after I stopped working` IS A BOOLEAN @desc After you ceased to work, are allowances, payments or other moneys payable to you by your employer or former employer as sick leave pay?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Could the Commission waive my waiting period because of sick leave pay` IF
    `reg 40(6) the conditions on which the Commission may waive the waiting period are met` `I qualify for benefits by an interruption of earnings from illness, injury, quarantine, pregnancy or care` `my employer or former employer pays me sick leave pay after I stopped working`

§ `Regulation 41 -- pregnancy`
-- Arises only for a person claiming because of pregnancy: ask 'Are you pregnant?'.

@export Have I given the Commission the proof of my pregnancy that regulation 41(1) requires?
GIVEN `I signed a statement attesting to my pregnancy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you signed a statement attesting to your pregnancy?
      `it declares my expected date of confinement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement declare your expected date of confinement?
      `my child has been born` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your child been born?
      `I told the Commission the actual date of the birth in person, by mail or by telephone` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you given the Commission information about the actual date of the birth, in person, by mail or by telephone?
      `I told it as soon as was reasonably possible after the birth` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you give that information as soon as was reasonably possible after the birth?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I given the Commission the proof of my pregnancy that is required` IF
    `reg 41(1) the information and evidence of pregnancy is given` `I signed a statement attesting to my pregnancy` `it declares my expected date of confinement` `my child has been born` `I told the Commission the actual date of the birth in person, by mail or by telephone` `I told it as soon as was reasonably possible after the birth`

@export Does my pregnancy count for the purposes of paragraph 8(2)(a) of the Act (regulation 41(2))?
GIVEN `I am pregnant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you pregnant?
      `it makes me incapable of doing the duties of my regular or usual employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the pregnancy make you incapable of performing the duties of your regular or usual employment?
      `it makes me incapable of doing the duties of other suitable employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the pregnancy make you incapable of performing the duties of other suitable employment?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my pregnancy count` IF
    `reg 41(2) pregnancy` `I am pregnant` `it makes me incapable of doing the duties of my regular or usual employment` `it makes me incapable of doing the duties of other suitable employment`

§ `Regulation 41.2 -- a medical certificate issued outside Canada`
-- Arises only for a person whose medical certificate was issued outside Canada.

@export Can a medical certificate issued outside Canada be accepted for my parental, compassionate care or critically ill child or adult benefits (regulation 41.2)?
GIVEN `the person who issued it is authorized abroad to do the work of a medical doctor or nurse practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the individual who issued the certificate authorized by the appropriate governmental authority of a country other than Canada to perform the work of a medical doctor or of a nurse practitioner?
      `their qualifications are substantially similar to those of a doctor or nurse practitioner in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does that individual have professional qualifications substantially similar to those of a medical doctor or nurse practitioner practising in Canada?
      `the person the certificate is about is in that country` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person to whom the certificate refers in that country?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can a medical certificate issued outside Canada be accepted` IF
    `reg 41.2 the medical certificate issued outside Canada may be accepted` `the person who issued it is authorized abroad to do the work of a medical doctor or nurse practitioner` `their qualifications are substantially similar to those of a doctor or nurse practitioner in Canada` `the person the certificate is about is in that country`

§ `Regulation 41.6 -- dividing the remaining weeks of benefits when the claimants cannot agree`
-- Arises only for a person who shares the weeks of parental, family or critical-illness care benefits with another claimant and they cannot agree on the division.

@export How many of the remaining weeks of benefits will I be paid when the claimants cannot agree (regulation 41.6)?
GIVEN `we cannot agree on a division of the remaining weeks` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the claimants sharing the remaining weeks of unpaid benefits fail to agree on a division?
      `a division is fixed by regulation 76.21(2) or 76.42(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the division fixed by regulation 76.21(2) or 76.42(2) (two claimants who live in different provinces, one claiming provincial benefits)?
      `the number of remaining weeks of unpaid benefits` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks of unpaid benefits remain to be divided?
      `the number of claimants sharing them` IS A NUMBER @desc How many claimants share them?
      `my place in the order in which we made our claims` IS A NUMBER @desc Counting the first claimant to make a claim as 1, what is your place in the order in which the claimants made their claims?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How many of the remaining weeks of benefits will I be paid` IS
    `reg 41.6 the weeks of benefits paid to the claimant` `we cannot agree on a division of the remaining weeks` `a division is fixed by regulation 76.21(2) or 76.42(2)` `the number of remaining weeks of unpaid benefits` `the number of claimants sharing them` `my place in the order in which we made our claims`

§ `Regulations 42 to 49 -- work-sharing benefits`
-- Arises only for a person employed in work-sharing employment under an agreement approved by the Commission: ask 'Is your employer on a work-sharing agreement?'.

@export Are work-sharing benefits payable to me for a week (regulation 42)?
GIVEN `I am employed in work-sharing employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed in work-sharing employment?
      `it is a week of unemployment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the week a week of unemployment?
      `the week falls in a benefit period established for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the week fall in a benefit period established for you?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are work-sharing benefits payable to me for the week` IF
    `reg 42 work-sharing benefits are payable for the week` `I am employed in work-sharing employment` `it is a week of unemployment` `the week falls in a benefit period established for me`

@export Has an interruption of my earnings occurred because my work-sharing hours cut my pay by at least 10 per cent (regulation 43)?
GIVEN `my normal weekly earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your normal weekly earnings, in dollars?
      `my earnings for the week` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your earnings for the week, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has an interruption of my earnings occurred because my pay was cut by at least 10 per cent` IS
    `reg 43 the reduction in the person's normal weekly earnings is at least 10 per cent` `my normal weekly earnings` `my earnings for the week`

@export On what day does my interruption of earnings occur under work-sharing (regulation 43)?
GIVEN `a day in the week in which my pay was cut` IS A DATE @desc Give any day in the week in which your pay was cut by at least 10 per cent (YYYY-MM-DD).
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On what day does my interruption of earnings occur under work-sharing` IS
    `reg 43 the day on which the interruption of earnings occurs` `a day in the week in which my pay was cut`

@export Am I not entitled to work-sharing benefits for a week because I claim regular benefits for it (regulation 44)?
GIVEN `I claim benefits under section 12 of the Act for the week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you claim regular benefits under section 12 of the Act for the same week?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I not entitled to work-sharing benefits for the week` IF
    `reg 44 the claimant is not entitled to work-sharing benefits for the week` `I claim benefits under section 12 of the Act for the week`

@export To what period is my benefit period extended for my weeks of work-sharing (regulation 45)?
GIVEN `the first day of my benefit period` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your benefit period begin (YYYY-MM-DD)?
      `the last day of my benefit period` IS A DATE @desc On what day does your benefit period end (YYYY-MM-DD)?
      `my weeks of work-sharing employment in it` IS A NUMBER @desc In how many weeks of the benefit period were you employed in work-sharing employment?
GIVETH A `Period of days`
DECIDE `To what period is my benefit period extended for my weeks of work-sharing` IS
    `reg 45 the benefit period as extended` (`Period of days` OF `the first day of my benefit period`, `the last day of my benefit period`) `my weeks of work-sharing employment in it`

@export Is serving my waiting period put off because I became employed in work-sharing employment (regulation 46)?
GIVEN `I became employed in work-sharing employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you become employed in work-sharing employment?
      `that employment has ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has that work-sharing employment ended?
      `I have not served my waiting period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you not yet served the waiting period section 13 of the Act requires?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is serving my waiting period put off because I became employed in work-sharing employment` IF
    `reg 46 the serving of the waiting period is deferred` `I became employed in work-sharing employment` `that employment has ended` `I have not served my waiting period`

@export Is the deduction of my earnings put off because I became employed in work-sharing employment (regulation 46)?
GIVEN `I became employed in work-sharing employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you become employed in work-sharing employment?
      `that employment has ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has that work-sharing employment ended?
      `my earnings have not been deducted as subsection 19(1) of the Act requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have your earnings not yet been deducted as subsection 19(1) of the Act requires?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the deduction of my earnings put off because I became employed in work-sharing employment` IF
    `reg 46 the deduction of earnings is deferred` `I became employed in work-sharing employment` `that employment has ended` `my earnings have not been deducted as subsection 19(1) of the Act requires`

@export How much will be deducted from my work-sharing benefits for a week because of my earnings (regulation 47)?
GIVEN `my earnings for the week from work-sharing employment` IS A NUMBER @desc How much did you earn for the week from work-sharing employment, in dollars?
      `I received other earnings for the week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you receive earnings for the week other than by reason of work-sharing employment?
      `the amount determined under subsection 19(2) of the Act` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount is determined under subsection 19(2) of the Act for those other earnings, in dollars? (0 if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much will be deducted from my work-sharing benefits for the week` IS
    (`reg 47(1) the amount of earnings from work-sharing employment deducted from the work-sharing benefits` `my earnings for the week from work-sharing employment`)
    PLUS (`reg 47(2) the amount deducted from the work-sharing benefits for the week` `I received other earnings for the week` `the amount determined under subsection 19(2) of the Act`)

@export What is my weekly rate of benefits under a work-sharing agreement (regulation 48)?
GIVEN `my rate of weekly benefits under section 14 of the Act` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your rate of weekly benefits determined under section 14 of the Act, in dollars?
      `the hours, days or shifts I did not work because of the work-sharing agreement` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours, days or shifts did you not work because of the work-sharing agreement?
      `the hours, days or shifts I would have worked on my usual schedule` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours, days or shifts would you have worked according to your usual work schedule (the same unit)?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my weekly rate of benefits under a work-sharing agreement` IS
    `reg 48 the rate of weekly benefits payable under a work-sharing agreement` `my rate of weekly benefits under section 14 of the Act` `the hours, days or shifts I did not work because of the work-sharing agreement` `the hours, days or shifts I would have worked on my usual schedule`

@export How many of my weeks of benefits count toward the maximum, leaving out my weeks of work-sharing (regulation 49)?
GIVEN `the weeks of benefits paid to me` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks of benefits have been paid to you in the benefit period?
      `the weeks of work-sharing benefits among them` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of those weeks were work-sharing benefits?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many of my weeks of benefits count toward the maximum` IS
    `reg 49 the weeks of benefits paid that count, not counting weeks of work-sharing benefits` `the weeks of benefits paid to me` `the weeks of work-sharing benefits among them`

§ `Regulations 50, 51 and 51.1 -- employment measures, work-force reduction, other reasonable circumstances`
-- Arises only for a person referred to an employment measure (50), who left a job under their employer's work-force reduction process (51), or left a job for one of the reasons of 51.1.

@export Is the measure I am referred to prescribed for the purposes of subparagraph 25(1)(b)(i) of the Act (regulation 50)?
GIVEN `it is an employment support measure of paragraph 59(b) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an employment support measure referred to in paragraph 59(b) of the Act?
      `it is the subject of an agreement under section 63 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a measure that is the subject of an agreement under section 63 of the Act?
      `it helps participants start businesses or become self-employed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it established to help insured participants start businesses or become self-employed?
      `it gives participants work experience to improve their long-term prospects` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it established to provide insured participants with employment opportunities through which they can gain work experience to improve their long-term employment prospects?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the measure I am referred to prescribed` IF
    `reg 50 the measure is prescribed for the purposes of subparagraph 25(1)(b)(i) of the Act` `it is an employment support measure of paragraph 59(b) of the Act` `it is the subject of an agreement under section 63 of the Act` `it helps participants start businesses or become self-employed` `it gives participants work experience to improve their long-term prospects`

@export May I be paid benefits although I left my job voluntarily under my employer's work-force reduction process (regulation 51)?
GIVEN `I left my employment in accordance with an employer work-force reduction process` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you leave your employment in accordance with an employer work-force reduction process?
      `my employer started the process` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the process initiated by your employer?
      `its objective is a permanent reduction in the number of employees` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is its objective a permanent reduction in the overall number of employees?
      `it offers employees the option to leave voluntarily` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it offer employees the option to leave employment voluntarily?
      `my employer documented all its elements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your employer documented its elements, including the three above?
      `the process preserves the jobs of co-workers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the process preserve the employment of co-workers?
      `I accepted an offer to leave voluntarily` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you accept an offer to leave that employment voluntarily?
      `my employer confirmed my leaving saved a co-worker's job` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your employer confirmed that your leaving resulted in the actual preservation of the employment of a co-worker whose employment would otherwise have been terminated?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I be paid benefits although I left voluntarily under a work-force reduction process` IF
    `reg 51(1) benefits may be paid notwithstanding section 30 of the Act to a claimant who left under a work-force reduction process` `I left my employment in accordance with an employer work-force reduction process` (`reg 51(2) employer work-force reduction process` `my employer started the process` `its objective is a permanent reduction in the number of employees` `it offers employees the option to leave voluntarily` `my employer documented all its elements`) `the process preserves the jobs of co-workers` `I accepted an offer to leave voluntarily` `my employer confirmed my leaving saved a co-worker's job`

@export Is my reason for leaving my job one of the other reasonable circumstances of regulation 51.1?
GIVEN `I must go with my partner of under a year to another residence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have an obligation to accompany to another residence a person with whom you had been living in a conjugal relationship?
      `the first day we lived together` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you begin living together in that relationship (YYYY-MM-DD)?
      `the day I left my job` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you leave your employment (YYYY-MM-DD)?
      `a child was born to or adopted by one of us in that time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did either of you have a child or adopt a child during that time?
      `one of us is expecting a child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is either of you expecting the birth of a child?
      `a child was placed with one of us for adoption in that time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a child placed with either of you during that time for the purpose of adoption?
      `I must care for someone` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have an obligation to care for a person?
      `that person's relationship to me` IS A `er3 Relationship of a person to the claimant` @desc What is that person's relationship to you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my reason for leaving my job one of the other reasonable circumstances` IS
    `reg 51.1 other reasonable circumstances include the circumstance`
        (`reg 51.1(a) an obligation to accompany a partner of less than one year to another residence` `I must go with my partner of under a year to another residence` `the first day we lived together` `the day I left my job` `a child was born to or adopted by one of us in that time` `one of us is expecting a child` `a child was placed with one of us for adoption in that time`)
        (`reg 51.1(b) an obligation to care for a member of the immediate family` `I must care for someone` `that person's relationship to me`)

§ `Regulations 52 and 53 -- a part-time job lost to a work stoppage, and the end of the stoppage`
-- Arises only for a person who lost a part-time job, or cannot resume it, because of a work stoppage: ask 'Did you lose a part-time job because of a strike or lock-out?'.

-- Only for a person whose part-time job was lost, or cannot be resumed, because of a stoppage of work caused by a labour dispute.
@export How many days of disentitlement do I have for the week because I lost a part-time job to a work stoppage (regulation 52)?
GIVEN `I lost a part-time job or cannot resume it because of a work stoppage under section 36(1) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you lose a part-time employment, or become unable to resume it, for a reason mentioned in subsection 36(1) of the Act (a stoppage of work)?
      `an event ending the stoppage for that job has occurred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an event referred to in paragraph 36(1)(a) or (b) of the Act occurred in respect of that part-time job?
      `my average weekly insurable earnings in that part-time job` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your average weekly insurable earnings in that part-time employment, in dollars?
      `my weekly insurable earnings under section 14 of the Act` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your weekly insurable earnings as determined under section 14 of the Act, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How many days of disentitlement do I have for the week` IS
    `reg 52 the days of disentitlement for the week` `I lost a part-time job or cannot resume it because of a work stoppage under section 36(1) of the Act` `an event ending the stoppage for that job has occurred` `my average weekly insurable earnings in that part-time job` `my weekly insurable earnings under section 14 of the Act`

@export Has the work stoppage at my workplace ended (regulation 53(1))?
GIVEN `the work-force level now` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the level of the work-force at the premises now (for example the number of employees)?
      `the part of it due to exceptional or temporary measures` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of that level is due to exceptional or temporary measures the employer took, before and during the stoppage, to offset its effects?
      `the normal work-force level` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the normal level of the work-force (the same unit)?
      `the activity level now` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the level of activity in the production of goods or services now (any one unit)?
      `the part of the activity due to exceptional or temporary measures` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of that activity is due to such exceptional or temporary measures?
      `the normal activity level` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the normal level of activity (the same unit)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the work stoppage at my workplace ended` IS
    `reg 53(1) the stoppage of work is terminated`
        (`reg 53 the level to be counted is at least 85 per cent of the normal level` `the work-force level now` `the part of it due to exceptional or temporary measures` `the normal work-force level`)
        (`reg 53 the level to be counted is at least 85 per cent of the normal level` `the activity level now` `the part of the activity due to exceptional or temporary measures` `the normal activity level`)

@export Has the work stoppage ended although an occurrence stopped it reaching 85 per cent of the normal level (regulation 53(2))?
GIVEN occurrence IS AN `er3 Occurrence preventing the attainment of the 85 per cent level` @desc What occurrence prevents the work-force or the activity from reaching 85 per cent of the normal level: a discontinuance of business, a permanent restructuring of activity, an act of God, a change in economic or market conditions, a change in technology, or none?
      `activity has resumed at the premises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has there been a resumption of activity at the premises?
      `the work-force is at 85 per cent of its adjusted normal level` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the work-force at least 85 per cent of its normal level as adjusted for the occurrence?
      `the activity is at 85 per cent of its adjusted normal level` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the level of activity at least 85 per cent of its normal level as adjusted for the occurrence?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the work stoppage ended although an occurrence prevented the 85 per cent level` IF
    `reg 53(2) the stoppage of work is terminated although an occurrence prevents the 85 per cent level` occurrence `activity has resumed at the premises` `the work-force is at 85 per cent of its adjusted normal level` `the activity is at 85 per cent of its adjusted normal level`

§ `Regulation 54 -- inmates of an institution`
-- Arises only for a person who is an inmate of a prison or similar institution.

@export Am I not disentitled by reason only of section 37 of the Act, as an inmate of an institution (regulation 54(1))?
GIVEN `I am self-employed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a self-employed person?
      `I am an inmate of a prison or similar institution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an inmate of a prison or similar institution?
      `what I have been granted` IS A `er3 Release granted to an inmate` @desc What have you been granted: parole, day parole, a temporary absence, a certificate of availability, or none?
      `it is for seeking and accepting employment in the community` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it granted for the purpose of seeking and accepting employment in the community?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I not disentitled by reason only of section 37 of the Act as an inmate` IF
    `reg 54(1) the claimant who is an inmate is not disentitled by reason only of section 37 of the Act` `I am self-employed` `I am an inmate of a prison or similar institution` `what I have been granted` `it is for seeking and accepting employment in the community`

@export As a self-employed person who is an inmate, am I not disentitled by reason only of section 152.2 of the Act (regulation 54(2))?
GIVEN `I am a self-employed person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a self-employed person?
      `I am an inmate of a prison or similar institution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an inmate of a prison or similar institution?
      `what I have been granted` IS A `er3 Release granted to an inmate` @desc What have you been granted: parole, day parole, a temporary absence, a certificate of availability, or none?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I not disentitled by reason only of section 152.2 of the Act as a self-employed inmate` IF
    `reg 54(2) the self-employed person who is an inmate is not disentitled by reason only of section 152.2 of the Act` `I am a self-employed person` `I am an inmate of a prison or similar institution` `what I have been granted`

§ `Regulations 55 and 55.01 -- outside Canada`
-- Arises only for a person who is, or will be, outside Canada while claiming: ask 'Are you outside Canada, or will you be, while you claim?'.

-- A person asks "Am I disentitled because I am outside Canada?" for a short stay of one of the six reasons.
@export Am I not disentitled because I am outside Canada for a short stay, as a claimant who is not self-employed (regulation 55(1))?
GIVEN `I am self-employed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a self-employed person?
      `the reason for my stay outside Canada` IS A `er3 Purpose of a stay outside Canada` @desc Why are you outside Canada: medical treatment for you, a funeral, accompanying a member of your immediate family for medical treatment, visiting a seriously ill or injured member of your immediate family, a bona fide job interview, a bona fide job search, or some other reason?
      `the consecutive days I am outside Canada` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many consecutive days are you outside Canada?
      `how that person is related to me` IS A `er3 Relationship of a person to the claimant` @desc If your stay is for a funeral, accompanying someone or visiting someone: how is that person related to you?
      `the treatment is not readily available in the area of residence in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If your stay is for medical treatment: is the treatment not readily or immediately available in the area of residence in Canada (yours, or the family member's)?
      `the facility is accredited abroad` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If your stay is for medical treatment: is the hospital, clinic or facility accredited to provide the treatment by the appropriate governmental authority outside Canada?
      `the family member is seriously ill or injured` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are visiting a family member: are they seriously ill or injured?
      `the interview or search is bona fide` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If your stay is for a job interview or a job search: is it bona fide?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I not disentitled because I am outside Canada for a short stay` IF
    `reg 55(1) the claimant who is not a self-employed person is not disentitled for the reason that they are outside Canada` `I am self-employed` `the reason for my stay outside Canada` `the consecutive days I am outside Canada` `how that person is related to me` `the treatment is not readily available in the area of residence in Canada` `the facility is accredited abroad` `the family member is seriously ill or injured` `the interview or search is bona fide`

@export Am I not disentitled because I am a self-employed person outside Canada for a short stay (regulation 55.01(1))?
GIVEN `I am a self-employed person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a self-employed person?
      `the reason for my stay outside Canada` IS A `er3 Purpose of a stay outside Canada` @desc Why are you outside Canada: medical treatment for you, a funeral, accompanying a member of your immediate family for medical treatment, visiting a seriously ill or injured member of your immediate family, or some other reason? (a job interview or a job search is not among the reasons for a self-employed person)
      `the consecutive days I am outside Canada` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many consecutive days are you outside Canada?
      `how that person is related to me` IS A `er3 Relationship of a person to the claimant` @desc If your stay is for a funeral, accompanying someone or visiting someone: how is that person related to you?
      `the treatment is not readily available in the area of residence in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If your stay is for medical treatment: is the treatment not readily or immediately available in the area of residence in Canada (yours, or the family member's)?
      `the facility is accredited abroad` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If your stay is for medical treatment: is the hospital, clinic or facility accredited to provide the treatment by the appropriate governmental authority outside Canada?
      `the family member is seriously ill or injured` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are visiting a family member: are they seriously ill or injured?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I, a self-employed person, not disentitled because I am outside Canada for a short stay` IF
    `reg 55.01(1) the self-employed person is not disentitled for the reason that they are outside Canada` `I am a self-employed person` `the reason for my stay outside Canada` `the consecutive days I am outside Canada` `how that person is related to me` `the treatment is not readily available in the area of residence in Canada` `the facility is accredited abroad` `the family member is seriously ill or injured`

@export For how many days may I be outside Canada on one trip for a funeral and a visit to the same person (regulation 55(1.1))?
GIVEN `my trip is for a funeral and for a visit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your trip both to attend a funeral and to visit a member of your immediate family?
      `the person I visit is the person whose funeral I attend` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person you visit the person whose funeral you attend?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `For how many days may I be outside Canada on one trip for a funeral and a visit` IS
    `reg 55(1.1) the most consecutive days of a single trip that cumulates the periods of paragraphs (1)(b) and (d)` `my trip is for a funeral and for a visit` `the person I visit is the person whose funeral I attend`

@export Is the person whose funeral I want to attend one for whom a short stay outside Canada is allowed (regulation 55(1)(b) and (2))?
GIVEN `how that person was related to me` IS A `er3 Relationship of a person to the claimant` @desc How was the person who died related to you?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the person whose funeral I want to attend one for whom a short stay is allowed` IF
    `reg 55(1)(b) a person whose funeral the claimant may attend` `how that person was related to me`

@export Is this person a member of my immediate family for regulations 55 and 55.01 (regulation 55(2))?
GIVEN `how that person is related to me` IS A `er3 Relationship of a person to the claimant` @desc How is that person related to you?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this person a member of my immediate family` IF
    `reg 55(2) a member of the claimant's immediate family` `how that person is related to me`

@export As a claimant, am I not disentitled for the sole reason that I am outside Canada while claiming pregnancy, child care, family care or similar benefits, or attending a course (regulation 55(4))?
GIVEN `I am self-employed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a self-employed person?
      `the reason for my benefits` IS A `Reason for benefits` @desc Why are you claiming benefits: pregnancy, caring for a new-born or adopted child, care or support of a family member, care of a critically ill child or adult, an illness, injury or quarantine, or something else?
      `I am attending a course or program of instruction or training referred to in paragraph 25(1)(a) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you attending a course or program of instruction or training you were referred to under paragraph 25(1)(a) of the Act?
      `my Social Insurance Number Card or its period of validity has expired` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your Social Insurance Number Card, or the period of validity of your Social Insurance Number, expired?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I not disentitled for the sole reason that I am outside Canada while claiming special benefits or attending a course` IF
    `reg 55(4) the claimant is not disentitled for the sole reason that they are outside Canada` `I am self-employed` `the reason for my benefits` `I am attending a course or program of instruction or training referred to in paragraph 25(1)(a) of the Act` `my Social Insurance Number Card or its period of validity has expired`

@export As a self-employed person, am I not disentitled for the sole reason that I am outside Canada while claiming pregnancy, child care, family care or similar benefits (regulation 55.01(3))?
GIVEN `I am a self-employed person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a self-employed person?
      `the reason for my benefits` IS A `Reason for benefits` @desc Why are you claiming benefits: pregnancy, caring for a new-born or adopted child, care or support of a family member, care of a critically ill child or adult, an illness, injury or quarantine, or something else?
      `my Social Insurance Number Card or its period of validity has expired` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your Social Insurance Number Card, or the period of validity of your Social Insurance Number, expired?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I, a self-employed person, not disentitled for the sole reason that I am outside Canada while claiming special benefits` IF
    `reg 55.01(3) the self-employed person is not disentitled for the sole reason that they are outside Canada` `I am a self-employed person` `the reason for my benefits` `my Social Insurance Number Card or its period of validity has expired`

@export Am I not disentitled for the sole reason that I am outside Canada, as a major attachment claimant who last worked abroad (regulation 55(5))?
GIVEN `I am a major attachment claimant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a major attachment claimant (600 hours or more of insurable employment in your qualifying period)?
      `I am a self-employed person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a self-employed person?
      `my most recent interruption of earnings was from insurable employment outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your most recent interruption of earnings before you made your claim from insurable employment outside Canada?
      `the reason for my benefits` IS A `Reason for benefits` @desc Why are you claiming benefits: pregnancy, caring for a new-born or adopted child, care or support of a family member, care of a critically ill child or adult, an illness, injury or quarantine, or something else?
      `I prove I am incapable of my regular or usual employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you prove that you are incapable, by reason of illness, injury or quarantine, of performing the duties of your regular or usual employment?
      `I prove I am incapable of other suitable employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you prove that you are incapable, by reason of illness, injury or quarantine, of performing the duties of other suitable employment?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I not disentitled for the sole reason that I am outside Canada as a major attachment claimant who last worked abroad` IF
    `reg 55(5) the major attachment claimant with the last interruption of earnings from insurable employment outside Canada is not disentitled for the sole reason that they are outside Canada` `I am a major attachment claimant` `I am a self-employed person` `my most recent interruption of earnings was from insurable employment outside Canada` `the reason for my benefits` `I prove I am incapable of my regular or usual employment` `I prove I am incapable of other suitable employment`

@export Am I not disentitled for the sole reason that I live outside Canada, in the United States (regulation 55(6))?
GIVEN `I am self-employed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a self-employed person?
      `I live outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you reside outside Canada?
      `I am a major attachment claimant under regulation 55(5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a major attachment claimant of the kind described in regulation 55(5) (your last interruption of earnings was from insurable employment outside Canada)?
      `I live in a state next to Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you reside temporarily or permanently in a state of the United States that is contiguous to Canada?
      `I am available for work in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you available for work in Canada?
      `I am able to report to an office of the Commission in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you able to report personally at an office of the Commission in Canada?
      `I do report when the Commission asks` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you report personally when the Commission asks?
      `I am qualified under Article VI of the 1942 Agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you qualified to receive benefits under Article VI of the Agreement between Canada and the United States respecting Unemployment Insurance, signed on March 6 and 12, 1942?
      `I live in the District of Columbia, Puerto Rico, the Virgin Islands or a state` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you reside temporarily or permanently in the District of Columbia, Puerto Rico, the Virgin Islands or any state of the United States?
      `the Commission has not suspended the Agreement there` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Commission not suspended the application of that Agreement for the place where you live?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I not disentitled for the sole reason that I live outside Canada` IF
    `reg 55(6) the claimant who resides outside Canada is not disentitled for the sole reason of their residence outside Canada` `I am self-employed` `I live outside Canada` `I am a major attachment claimant under regulation 55(5)` (`reg 55(6)(a) the claimant resides in a state contiguous to Canada, is available and reports when requested` `I live in a state next to Canada` `I am available for work in Canada` `I am able to report to an office of the Commission in Canada` `I do report when the Commission asks`) (`reg 55(6)(b) the claimant is qualified under Article VI of the Canada-United States Agreement and resides in a place where it applies` `I am qualified under Article VI of the 1942 Agreement` `I live in the District of Columbia, Puerto Rico, the Virgin Islands or a state` `the Commission has not suspended the Agreement there`)

@export What is the most weeks of benefits I may be paid while I am outside Canada (regulation 55(7))?
GIVEN `my benefits are for a reason mentioned in subsection 12(3) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are your benefits paid for a reason mentioned in subsection 12(3) of the Act (pregnancy, child care, illness, family care and so on) rather than regular benefits?
      `the weeks that subsections 12(3) to (6) of the Act give for that reason` IS A NUMBER @desc If so: how many weeks do subsections 12(3) to (6) of the Act give for that reason?
      `my hours of insurable employment in my qualifying period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours of insurable employment did you have in your qualifying period?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most weeks of benefits I may be paid while I am outside Canada` IS
    `reg 55(7) the maximum number of weeks of benefits for a claimant not in Canada` `my benefits are for a reason mentioned in subsection 12(3) of the Act` `the weeks that subsections 12(3) to (6) of the Act give for that reason` `my hours of insurable employment in my qualifying period`

@export How many more weeks may I be paid now that I live in Canada again (regulation 55(8))?
GIVEN `the most weeks I could be paid while outside Canada` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the maximum number of weeks for which you could be paid under regulation 55(7)?
      `the weeks already paid to me` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks have already been paid to you?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many more weeks may I be paid now that I live in Canada again` IS
    `reg 55(8) the weeks for which the claimant who becomes resident in Canada continues to be entitled` `the most weeks I could be paid while outside Canada` `the weeks already paid to me`

@export What is the most weeks I may be paid after I move to the United States from Canada (regulation 55(9))?
GIVEN `the weeks I already received in Canada` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many weeks have you already received benefits in Canada?
      `the weeks I would have had if I had lived there when my benefit period began` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks would you have been entitled to under regulation 55(7) had you resided in the place referred to in regulation 55(6) when your benefit period was established?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most weeks I may be paid after I move to the United States` IS
    `reg 55(9) the maximum number of weeks of benefits for a claimant who becomes a claimant referred to in subsection (6)` `the weeks I already received in Canada` `the weeks I would have had if I had lived there when my benefit period began`

@export How many weeks of different benefits may I combine while I am outside Canada (regulation 55(10))?
GIVEN `my benefit period is extended under subsection 10(13) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your benefit period been extended under subsection 10(13) of the Act?
      `the maximum weeks calculated under subsection 10(15) of the Act` IS A NUMBER @desc If extended: what is the maximum number of weeks calculated under subsection 10(15) of the Act? (0 if not extended)
      `the weeks I am entitled to of each kind of benefit` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc For each kind of benefit, how many weeks are you entitled to (each within its own maximum under regulation 55(7))? (one number per kind)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many weeks of different benefits may I combine while outside Canada` IS
    `reg 55(10) the weeks of benefits that may be combined` `the weeks I am entitled to of each kind of benefit` (`reg 55(10) the most weeks that may be combined` `my benefit period is extended under subsection 10(13) of the Act` `the maximum weeks calculated under subsection 10(15) of the Act`)

@export Am I not disentitled for the sole reason that I am outside Canada in the course of my employment under an employment measure (regulation 55(11))?
GIVEN `I am self-employed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a self-employed person?
      `the Commission approved my being outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you outside Canada with the approval of the Commission?
      `it is in the course of my employment under a measure of paragraph 59(b) or an agreement under section 63` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it in the course of your employment under an employment support measure referred to in paragraph 59(b) of the Act, or a measure that is the subject of an agreement under section 63 of the Act?
      `that measure is to help participants start businesses or become self-employed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that measure established to help insured participants start businesses or become self-employed?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I not disentitled for the sole reason that I am outside Canada in the course of my employment under a measure` IF
    `reg 55(11) the claimant is not disentitled for the sole reason that they are outside Canada in the course of employment under a measure` `I am self-employed` `the Commission approved my being outside Canada` `it is in the course of my employment under a measure of paragraph 59(b) or an agreement under section 63` `that measure is to help participants start businesses or become self-employed`

@export Is the way I am sending my claim from outside Canada the way regulation 55(12) requires?
GIVEN `my claim is in an envelope or package addressed to the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your claim sent in an envelope or package addressed to the Commission?
      `I send it by mail` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you send it by mail?
      `I send it by certified mail` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you send it by certified mail?
      `I send it by registered mail` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you send it by registered mail?
      `I send it by another delivery service that provides proof of delivery` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you send it by another delivery service that provides proof of delivery?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I sending my claim from outside Canada in the manner required` IF
    `reg 55(12) the claim is sent in the manner required` `my claim is in an envelope or package addressed to the Commission` `I send it by mail` `I send it by certified mail` `I send it by registered mail` `I send it by another delivery service that provides proof of delivery`

@export Will my claim sent from outside Canada be reviewed by an employee of the Commission at the time of importation (regulation 55(13))?
GIVEN `my claim is in an envelope or package addressed to the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your claim sent in an envelope or package addressed to the Commission?
      `I send it by mail` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you send it by mail?
      `I send it by certified mail` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you send it by certified mail?
      `I send it by registered mail` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you send it by registered mail?
      `I send it by another delivery service that provides proof of delivery` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you send it by another delivery service that provides proof of delivery?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Will my claim sent from outside Canada be reviewed at importation` IF
    `reg 55(13) the claim is reviewed by an employee of the Commission at the time of importation` (`reg 55(12) the claim is sent in the manner required` `my claim is in an envelope or package addressed to the Commission` `I send it by mail` `I send it by certified mail` `I send it by registered mail` `I send it by another delivery service that provides proof of delivery`)

§ `Regulations 55.1 and 55.2 -- what my employer tells the Commission, and amounts paid to me while not entitled`
-- Arises only for a person whose employer takes part in the Commission's verification program (55.1), or who was paid benefits for a week for which they were not entitled (55.2).

@export What will my employer tell the Commission about me each month (regulation 55.1)?
GIVEN `my employer takes part in the Commission's program to substantiate claimants' proof` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your employer participate in a program that enables the Commission to substantiate proof given by claimants of their fulfilment of conditions for receiving or continuing to receive benefits?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many kinds of information will my employer tell the Commission about me each month` IS
    count (`reg 55.1 the information the employer provides about each employee each month` `my employer takes part in the Commission's program to substantiate claimants' proof`)

@export Could the Commission ratify the benefits I was paid while I was not entitled (regulation 55.2)?
GIVEN `the day my benefit period was established` IS A DATE @desc On what day was your benefit period established (YYYY-MM-DD)?
      `it followed a claim for special benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your benefit period established following a claim for special benefits?
      `the week is after my benefit period should have expired` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the week for which you were paid after the expiry of the benefit period that should have been established for you under subsection 10(2) of the Act as it read on October 25, 2009?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Could the Commission ratify the benefits I was paid while I was not entitled` IF
    `reg 55.2 the amount paid for the week is one the Commission may ratify` `the day my benefit period was established` `it followed a claim for special benefits` `the week is after my benefit period should have expired`

§ `Regulation 56 -- what I owe, and whether it can be written off`
-- Arises only for a person who owes the Crown a penalty or an amount wrongly paid: ask 'Do you owe the Commission money?'.

-- Only for a person who owes the Crown a penalty or an amount wrongly paid (an overpayment).
@export Could the Commission write off a penalty, an amount I owe, or the interest on it (regulation 56(1))?
GIVEN `it is a penalty or an amount payable under the sections regulation 56(1) lists, or interest on one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a penalty owing under section 38, 39 or 65.1 of the Act, an amount payable under section 43, 45, 46, 46.1 or 65, or the interest accrued on one of them?
      `all I owe the Crown under any program of the Department, with interest` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total of the penalties and amounts, with the interest accrued, that you owe Her Majesty under any program administered by the Department of Employment and Social Development, in dollars?
      `a benefit period is running for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a benefit period currently running in respect of you?
      `I am making regular payments on a repayment plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you currently making regular payments on a repayment plan?
      `the debtor is deceased` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the debtor died?
      `the debtor is a discharged bankrupt` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the debtor a discharged bankrupt?
      `the debtor is an undischarged bankrupt` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the debtor an undischarged bankrupt?
      `the final dividend has been paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the final dividend been paid?
      `the trustee has been discharged` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the trustee been discharged?
      `the overpayment arose from my error` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the overpayment arise from an error you made?
      `the overpayment arose from a false or misleading declaration of mine` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it arise from a false or misleading declaration or representation you made, whether or not you knew it to be false or misleading?
      `it arose from a retrospective decision or ruling under Part IV of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it arise from a retrospective decision or ruling made under Part IV of the Act?
      `it arose from a retrospective decision under Part I or IV on benefits paid under section 25` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it arise from a retrospective decision made under Part I or IV of the Act in relation to benefits paid under section 25?
      `the Commission considers it uncollectable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Commission consider, having regard to all the circumstances, that it is uncollectable?
      `the Commission considers that repaying it would cause me undue hardship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Commission consider that repaying it would cause you undue hardship?
      `the Commission considers that collecting it would cost as much as it is worth` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Commission consider that the administrative costs of collecting it would likely equal or exceed what is to be collected?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Could the Commission write off a penalty, an amount I owe, or the interest on it` IF
    `reg 56(1) the conditions on which the Commission may write off a penalty, an amount payable or the interest are met` `it is a penalty or an amount payable under the sections regulation 56(1) lists, or interest on one`
        (`reg 56(1)(a) the amounts owing do not exceed $100 and the debtor has no benefit period running and no repayment plan` `all I owe the Crown under any program of the Department, with interest` `a benefit period is running for me` `I am making regular payments on a repayment plan`)
        `the debtor is deceased` `the debtor is a discharged bankrupt`
        (`reg 56(1)(d) the debtor is an undischarged bankrupt whose final dividend has been paid and whose trustee has been discharged` `the debtor is an undischarged bankrupt` `the final dividend has been paid` `the trustee has been discharged`)
        (`reg 56(1)(e) the overpayment arises from a retrospective decision and not from the debtor's error or false declaration` `the overpayment arose from my error` `the overpayment arose from a false or misleading declaration of mine` `it arose from a retrospective decision or ruling under Part IV of the Act` `it arose from a retrospective decision under Part I or IV on benefits paid under section 25`)
        (`reg 56(1)(f) the Commission considers it uncollectable, a hardship or not worth collecting` `the Commission considers it uncollectable` `the Commission considers that repaying it would cause me undue hardship` `the Commission considers that collecting it would cost as much as it is worth`)

@export How much of an overpayment for benefits received more than 12 months before I was notified could be written off (regulation 56(2))?
GIVEN `the day I received the older benefit` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you receive the benefits that were overpaid (YYYY-MM-DD)?
      `the overpayment in respect of it` IS A NUMBER @desc How much was overpaid in respect of those benefits, in dollars?
      `the day the Commission notified me of the overpayment` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the Commission notify you of the overpayment (YYYY-MM-DD)?
      `the interest accrued on that portion` IS A NUMBER @desc How much interest has accrued on that portion, in dollars?
      `the overpayment arose from my error` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the overpayment arise from an error you made?
      `the overpayment arose from a false or misleading declaration of mine` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it arise from a false or misleading declaration or representation you made?
      `a delay or error by the Commission in processing my claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it arise from a delay or error made by the Commission in processing your claim for benefits?
      `retrospective control procedures or a review by the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it arise from retrospective control procedures or a retrospective review initiated by the Commission?
      `an error on my record of employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it arise from an error made on the record of employment by your employer?
      `an incorrect calculation by my employer of my insurable earnings or hours` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it arise from an incorrect calculation by your employer of your insurable earnings or hours of insurable employment?
      `an error in insuring my employment or other activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it arise from an error in insuring your employment or other activity?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of an overpayment for benefits received more than 12 months before I was notified could be written off` IS
    `reg 56(2) the portion of the amount owing that may be written off` (LIST (`er3 Overpaid benefit` OF `the day I received the older benefit`, `the overpayment in respect of it`)) `the day the Commission notified me of the overpayment` `the interest accrued on that portion` (`reg 56(2)(a) the overpayment does not arise from the debtor's error or false declaration` `the overpayment arose from my error` `the overpayment arose from a false or misleading declaration of mine`) (`reg 56(2)(b) the overpayment arises as a result of one of the five causes` `a delay or error by the Commission in processing my claim` `retrospective control procedures or a review by the Commission` `an error on my record of employment` `an incorrect calculation by my employer of my insurable earnings or hours` `an error in insuring my employment or other activity`)

§ `Regulation 56.1 -- interest on what I owe`
-- Arises only for a person who owes the Crown a debt on which interest may run: ask 'Do you owe the Commission money?'.

@export Does interest run on the debt I owe (regulation 56.1(1) to (3))?
GIVEN `it is an amount payable under section 43, 45, 46, 46.1 or 65 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the debt an amount payable under section 43, 45, 46, 46.1 or 65 of the Act?
      `a penalty was imposed on me under section 38, 39 or 65.1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a penalty imposed on you under section 38, 39 or 65.1 of the Act in respect of it?
      `a warning was issued to me under section 41.1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a warning issued to you under section 41.1 of the Act in respect of it?
      `I was prosecuted under section 135 or 136 or the Criminal Code` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a prosecution undertaken against you under section 135 or 136 of the Act or under the Criminal Code in respect of it?
      `the debt is an amount payable under section 38, 39 or 65.1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the debt itself an amount payable under section 38, 39 or 65.1 of the Act?
      `the debt is payable as a result of a court judgment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the debt an amount payable as a result of the judgment of a court?
      `my penalty or warning was rescinded on appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did an appeal result in the rescinding of the penalty or warning?
      `I was acquitted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you eventually acquitted in a prosecution under section 135 or 136 of the Act or under the Criminal Code?
      `the debt is owing to Her Majesty under section 47 or 65.2 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the debt owing to Her Majesty under section 47 or 65.2 of the Act?
      `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc For which day do you ask (YYYY-MM-DD)?
      `the day regulation 56.1 came into force` IS A DATE @desc On what day did regulation 56.1 come into force (YYYY-MM-DD)? (the text of the Regulations does not say; ask the Commission)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does interest run on the debt I owe` IF
    `reg 56.1(3) the debt carries interest` `the debt is a debt arising from an act or omission` `the debt is owing to Her Majesty under section 47 or 65.2 of the Act` `the day I ask about` `the day regulation 56.1 came into force`
    WHERE
        `the debt is a debt arising from an act or omission` MEANS
                `reg 56.1(1) debt arising from an act or omission, before subsection (2)` `it is an amount payable under section 43, 45, 46, 46.1 or 65 of the Act` `a penalty was imposed on me under section 38, 39 or 65.1` `a warning was issued to me under section 41.1` `I was prosecuted under section 135 or 136 or the Criminal Code` `the debt is an amount payable under section 38, 39 or 65.1` `the debt is payable as a result of a court judgment`
            AND NOT (`reg 56.1(2) the debt is not a debt arising from an act or omission` `my penalty or warning was rescinded on appeal` `I was acquitted`)

@export How much interest runs on my debt for a month (regulation 56.1(3))?
GIVEN `the bank rates established during the month before` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc What were the Bank of Canada's bank rates established during the month before the month for which interest is calculated, as fractions (4.25% is 0.0425)? (one number per rate)
      `what I owe at the start of the month` IS A NUMBER @desc What do you owe at the start of the month, including interest already added, in dollars?
      `the days of the month` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days has the month?
      `the days of the year` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days of the year is the daily interest counted on? (the Regulations do not say; 365 is the usual figure)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much interest runs on my debt for a month` IS
    CONSIDER `reg 56.1(3) the annual rate of interest` (`reg 56.1(1) the average bank rate` `the bank rates established during the month before`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST rate THEN `reg 56.1(3) the interest accruing in a month` `what I owe at the start of the month` rate `the days of the month` `the days of the year`

@export On what day does the interest on my debt begin to run (regulation 56.1(4))?
GIVEN `the day I was notified of the amount I owe` IS A DATE @desc On what day were you notified of the amount owing (YYYY-MM-DD)?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On what day does the interest on my debt begin to run` IS
    `reg 56.1(4) the day on which interest begins to accrue` `the day I was notified of the amount I owe`

@export Does interest stop running on my debt while my appeal or review is pending (regulation 56.1(5) and (6))?
GIVEN `an appeal or review of the decision that gave rise to my debt is pending` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is an appeal or other review of the decision that gave rise to the obligation to pay pending?
      `all that is pending is the Commission reconsidering a decision under section 41, 52 or 111` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the only thing pending the Commission's reconsideration of a decision under section 41, 52 or 111 of the Act?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does interest stop running on my debt while my appeal is pending` IF
    `reg 56.1(5) and (6) interest does not accrue because an appeal or review is pending` `an appeal or review of the decision that gave rise to my debt is pending` `all that is pending is the Commission reconsidering a decision under section 41, 52 or 111`

@export On what day does the interest on my debt stop running (regulation 56.1(7))?
GIVEN `my repayment and the interest have been received` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has repayment of the amount owed and the accrued interest been received by Her Majesty or a duly authorized agent?
      `the day they were received` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what day (YYYY-MM-DD)?
      `the debtor has died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the debtor died?
      `the day the debtor died` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what day (YYYY-MM-DD)?
      `the amount owed has been written off under section 56` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the amount owed been written off under section 56?
      `the day the amount was written off` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what day (YYYY-MM-DD)?
      `the accrued interest has been written off under section 56` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the accrued interest been written off under section 56?
      `the day the interest was written off` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what day (YYYY-MM-DD)?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On what day does the interest on my debt stop running` IS
    `reg 56.1(7) the day on which the accrual of interest ceases`
        (IF `my repayment and the interest have been received` THEN JUST `the day they were received` ELSE NOTHING)
        (IF `the debtor has died` THEN JUST `the day the debtor died` ELSE NOTHING)
        (IF `the amount owed has been written off under section 56` THEN JUST `the day the amount was written off` ELSE NOTHING)
        (IF `the accrued interest has been written off under section 56` THEN JUST `the day the interest was written off` ELSE NOTHING)

@export Does interest run on my debt on a given day (regulation 56.1(3) to (7))?
GIVEN `interest runs on my kind of debt under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does interest run on the debt under regulation 56.1(3) (see the question about whether interest runs on it)?
      `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc For which day do you ask (YYYY-MM-DD)?
      `the day I was notified of the amount I owe` IS A DATE @desc On what day were you notified of the amount owing (YYYY-MM-DD)?
      `an appeal or review of the decision that gave rise to my debt is pending` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is an appeal or other review of the decision that gave rise to the obligation to pay pending?
      `all that is pending is the Commission reconsidering a decision under section 41, 52 or 111` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the only thing pending the Commission's reconsideration of a decision under section 41, 52 or 111 of the Act?
      `interest has stopped running on a day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an event happened that stops the interest from running (repayment, the debtor's death, a write-off)?
      `the day it stopped` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what day (YYYY-MM-DD)? (the day itself is the first day without interest)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does interest run on my debt on a given day` IF
    `reg 56.1 interest accrues on the day` `interest runs on my kind of debt under subsection (3)` `the day I ask about` (`reg 56.1(4) the day on which interest begins to accrue` `the day I was notified of the amount I owe`) (`reg 56.1(5) and (6) interest does not accrue because an appeal or review is pending` `an appeal or review of the decision that gave rise to my debt is pending` `all that is pending is the Commission reconsidering a decision under section 41, 52 or 111`) (IF `interest has stopped running on a day` THEN JUST `the day it stopped` ELSE NOTHING)

@export Could the Commission waive or reduce the interest I owe (regulation 56.1(8))?
GIVEN `what it would cost the Commission to collect the interest` IS A NUMBER @desc What would the administrative costs of collecting the interest owing be, in dollars?
      `the interest I owe` IS A NUMBER @desc How much interest do you owe, in dollars?
      `the interest is on an amount in dispute that was settled in my favour` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the interest payable on an amount in dispute, where the dispute has been settled, in whole or in part, in your favour?
      `the interest would cause me undue hardship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the accrual of interest on the penalty or amount result in undue hardship to you?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Could the Commission waive or reduce the interest I owe` IF
    `reg 56.1(8) the conditions on which the Commission may waive or reduce the interest are met` `what it would cost the Commission to collect the interest` `the interest I owe` `the interest is on an amount in dispute that was settled in my favour` `the interest would cause me undue hardship`

§ `Regulation 57 -- deductions from my benefits for welfare and advances`
-- Arises only for a person who received an advance, assistance or welfare payment from a government.

@export Can an amount be deducted from my benefits for an advance, assistance or welfare payment I received (regulation 57)?
GIVEN `it is an advance, assistance or welfare payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the payment an advance, assistance or welfare payment?
      `who paid it` IS A `er3 Payer of an advance, assistance or welfare payment` @desc Who paid it: the Government of Canada or one of its agencies, a provincial government, a municipal government, the council of an Indian band, or someone else?
      `the Commission has an arrangement with the payer about the deduction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Commission entered into an arrangement with the payer in respect of the deduction?
      `the Commission has ended that arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Commission terminated that arrangement?
      `I signed the Commission's consent form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you consented to the deduction under subsection 42(3) of the Act by signing the form the Commission supplied?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can an amount be deducted from my benefits for an advance, assistance or welfare payment` IS
    `reg 57(2) a deduction may be made from the benefits in respect of the payment` `it is an advance, assistance or welfare payment` `who paid it` (`reg 57(3) the arrangement is in force` `the Commission has an arrangement with the payer about the deduction` `the Commission has ended that arrangement`) `I signed the Commission's consent form`
